\p
\v 14 After¦5310 Lot¦5313 had left, Yahweh¦5305 told Abram¦5309, “Look¦5318 all around you¦5324 towards the north¦5326, the south¦5327, the east, and¦5305 the west,
\v 15 because¦5331 all¦5334 that land¦5336 that you can see¦5340, I'll¦5332 give¦5342 it¦5342 to you and¦5343 to your¦5343 descendants to have forever¦5346.\x + \xo 13:15: \xt Acts 7:5.\x*
\v 16 I'll¦5348 make¦5348 your descendants \add as numerous\add* as dust \add particles\add*. Your descendants will¦5358 only be able to be counted¦5360 if¦5356 someone's able to count¦5360 all the dust \add particles\add* on the earth¦5364.
\v 17 \add So,\add* go and \add start\add* walking¦5371 throughout the¦5372 land—through its length¦5373 and its width, because¦5375 I'm giving¦5377 it¦5377 \add all\add* to¦5376 you.”
\v 18 \add So\add* Abram¦5380 moved¦5379 his tents¦5379 and went¦5381 and settled by the¦5383 terebinth trees¦5383 at¦5383 Mamre¦5384 (near Hebron¦5386), and he¦5387 built¦5387 an¦5390 altar¦5390 to¦5391 Yahweh¦5391 there¦5389.
\c 14
\s1 Five kings defend against four attackers
