\p
\v 1 At the time¦5395 when Amrafel¦5396 was king of Shinar¦5399, Arioch¦5400 was king of Ellasar¦5402, Kedorlaomer¦5403 was king of Elam¦5405, and¦5406 Tidal¦5406 was king of the Goyim¦5408,
\v 2 they¦5410 went to war¦5411 against Bera¦5414 king of Sodom¦5416, Birsha¦5419 king of Amorah¦5421 \add !(Gomorrah¦5421)\add*, Shinab¦5422 king of Admah¦5425, Shemeber¦5426 king of Tsevoim¦5428, and¦5431 the¦5431 king of Bela¦5432 (also¦5417 known as Tso'ar¦5435).
\v 3 Those latter five kings joined¦5440 forces in the Siddim¦5444 valley (also known as the Salt¦5447 Sea¦5446 valley).
\v 4 They¦5452 had¦5452 been subject to King Kedorlaomer¦5455 for twelve years¦5451, but¦5456 in the thirteenth year¦5459 they¦5460 rebelled¦5460.
\p
\v 5 Then¦5462 in the fourteenth year¦5464, Kedorlaomer¦5466 and the kings¦5467 who¦5468 were with¦5462 him¦5469 went¦5465 and attacked the Refaim¦5473 in Ashteroth¦5474-Karnaim, and the Zuzim¦5478 in Ham¦5479, and the Emim¦5481 in Shaveh¦5482-Kiriathaim¦5483,
\v 6 and¦5485 the Horites¦5487 in¦5488 the hill¦5488 country¦5488 of¦5488 Se'ir¦5489 as far as El¦5491 Paran¦5492, which¦5493 is¦5494 near the wilderness¦5496.
\v 7 Then¦5498 \add those four kings\add* turned¦5498 back¦5498 and went¦5499 to¦5500 En¦5502 Mishpat¦5503 (also called Kadesh¦5505) and they¦5499 attacked the entire¦5509 territories of¦5511 the Amalekites¦5512 and also the Amorites¦5516, who¦5517 were living¦5517 in¦5518 Hazezon¦5518 Tamar.
\p
\v 8 Then¦5521 the king of Sodom¦5524, the king of Amorah¦5526 \add !(Gomorrah¦5526)\add*, the king of Admah¦5528, the king of Tsevoim¦5530, and the king of Bela¦5533 (also¦5525 called Zoar¦5536) went¦5521 out¦5521 into the Siddim¦5541 Valley¦5540 and arranged \add their troops\add* for battle¦5539
\v 9 against Kedorlaomer¦5544 king of Elam¦5546, Tidal¦5547 king of Goiim¦5549, Amrafel¦5550 king of Shinar¦5552, Arioch¦5553 king of Ellasar¦5555—five¦5560 kings¦5557 \add defending themselves\add* against the¦5560 four¦5556.
\v 10 Now the Siddim¦5563 Valley¦5562 had many tar pits, and when the kings¦5569 of¦5569 Sodom¦5571 and Amorah¦5572 \add !(Gomorrah¦5572)\add* fled, they¦5578 fell¦5573 into the pits, \add but\add* the rest fled up into the hills.
\v 11 Then¦5580 \add the four attacking kings\add* took¦5580 all the \add peoples'\add* possessions¦5585 from Sodom¦5586 and Amorah¦5587 \add !(Gomorrah¦5587)\add* and all their¦5592 food¦5592 and left.
\s1 Abram rescues Lot
