\v 12 Abram's¦5605 nephew Lot¦5598 and¦5595 all his¦5601 possessions¦5601 also¦5599 got taken¦5595 because he¦5607 was¦5608 living¦5608 in¦5609 \add the city of\add* Sodom¦5609,
\v 13 \add but\add* someone who escaped¦5612 came¦5611 and reported \add this news\add* to¦5614 Abram the Hebrew¦5615. \add At that time,\add* Abram was¦5617 \add still\add* living¦5617 by the terebinth trees¦5618 of Mamre¦5619 the Amorite¦5620, the brother of Eshcol¦5622 and the brother of Aner¦5624, and the three of them had formed an alliance \add together\add*.
\v 14 When¦5637 Abram¦5632 heard that¦5633 his nephew had¦5634 been taken¦5634 captive¦5634, he led out¦5636 his 318 trained¦5639 men¦5639 who'd \add all\add* been born¦5640 in his house¦5641, and¦5631 he pursued¦5646 his enemies as far as \add the town of\add* Dan¦5649.
\v 15 During the night¦5654, Abram split in his¦5656 slaves into groups and they attacked¦5657 \add the four kings and their soldiers\add* and pursued¦5658 them¦5658 to¦5659 Hobah¦5661 (north¦5663 of¦5664 Damascus¦5664).
\v 16 They were able to bring back¦5666 all¦5668 the possessions, as well as his nephew Lot¦5674 and his possessions, and also¦5678 the women¦5681 and the \add other\add* people¦5684 \add who'd been captured\add*.
