\v 22 \add But\add* Abram¦5766 said¦5765 to¦5767 the king¦5769 of Sodom¦5770, “I¦5771 promise by Yahweh¦5775, most high God¦5776, the owner of heaven¦5779 and¦5765 earth¦5780,
\v 23 that I¦5791 won't take¦5791 anything of yours, not¦5797 even the strap of a sandal¦5788, so that you won't \add be able to\add* say¦5798 that it was you who made¦5800 me wealthy¦5800.
\v 24 I'll \add take\add* nothing, except what the young¦5809 \add fighters\add* have¦5808 eaten¦5808, and the share of¦5810 the other men¦5811 who¦5812 went¦5813 with¦5814 me¦5814: Aner¦5815, Eshcol¦5816, and Mamre¦5817. Let¦5819 them¦5819 take their¦5820 share.”
\c 15
\s1 God agreement with Abram
\rem /s1 The Lord's Covenant with Abram; God's Covenant With Abram; God's Covenant with Abram; The Lord's covenant with Abram
\p
\v 1 After¦5823 those¦5826 events, Yahweh¦5830 spoke to¦5831 Abram in¦5834 a vision¦5834, telling him, “Don't¦5836 be¦5844 afraid, Abram, because I'll protect you and I'll generously and richly reward¦5843 you.”
\p
\v 2 “My¦5856 master¦5849 Yahweh¦5850,” replied¦5847 Abram¦5848, “what¦5851 will¦5853 you¦5853 give¦5853 me¦5855, since we have no children¦5858 and¦5847 it's¦5847 Eliezer¦5865 (\add my chief slave\add* from Damascus¦5864) who'll inherit all my possessions?”
\v 3 Then¦5867 he¦5867 continued¦5867, “\add Yes,\add* you¦5872 haven't given¦5872 me¦5870 a child so wow, my heir is¦5878 a slave from my household¦5877!”
\p
\v 4 Then¦5881 listen, Yahweh's¦5884 word¦5882 came¦5894 to¦5885 \add Abram\add* saying¦5886, “That¦5893 man won't¦5887 be your heir, but¦5881 on the¦5882 contrary, it'll be your biological son.”
\v 5 Then \add Yahweh\add* took \add Abram\add* outside¦5901 and said, “Look¦5903 up at the sky and see if¦5909 you¦5911 can count¦5912 the stars¦5908.” Then he¦5914 said to¦5915 him¦5915, “Your¦5918 descendants will¦5917 be¦5917 like that.”\x + \xo 15:5: \xt Rom 4:18; Heb 11:12.\x*
\p
\v 6 \add Abram\add* believed¦5920 in¦5921 Yahweh, and¦5922 \add Yahweh considered that faith of Abram's as an act of obedience\add*.\x + \xo 15:6: \xt Rom 4:3; Gal 3:6; Jam 2:23.\x*
\p
\v 7 Then¦5926 Yahweh told \add Abram\add*, “I'm¦5928 Yahweh who¦5930 brought¦5931 you out¦5931 of¦5933 Ur¦5932 (where the¦5933 Chaldeans¦5933 lived) so I could give¦5934 you this¦5939 land¦5938 to¦5940 possess¦5940 it¦5940.”
\p
\v 8 “My¦5943 master¦5943 Yahweh¦5944,” Abram asked, “how¦5945 will I know¦5946 that¦5947 I will possess¦5948 it¦5948?”
\p
\v 9 “Bring¦5952 me¦5953 a three-year-old heifer¦5954,” Yahweh replied¦5950, “and a three-year-old she-goat and a three-year-old ram¦5958 and a turtledove¦5960 and a young¦5961 pigeon¦5961.”
\v 10 So¦5963 \add Abram\add* brought all¦5968 those¦5970 to \add Yahweh\add*, and then¦5963 he¦5985 cut¦5971 the animals (but¦5963 not¦5984 the birds¦5982) in¦5973 half down the middle¦5973 and laid the halves opposite¦5978 to each¦5968 other.
\v 11 Then¦5993 \add some\add* birds¦5988 of prey¦5988 flew down to the¦5988 carcasses¦5991, \add but\add* Abram¦5994 shooed them¦5993 away¦5992.
\p
\v 12 Later¦6004 as the¦5997 sun¦5997 was¦5996 going¦5998 down, Abram¦6003 fell¦6000 into a deep¦5999 sleep¦5999, and it¦6000 suddenly became completely dark and he¦5996 became terrified,\x + \xo 15:12: \xt Yob 4:13-14.\x*
\v 13 and \add Yahweh\add* said¦6011 to Abram¦6012, “Know¦6013 for certain¦6013 that your descendants will be¦6019 strangers in¦6021 a land that doesn't belong to them, and they'll¦6024 serve¦6024 the \add rulers of that land\add* and \add those rulers\add* will persecute them for 400 years¦6029.\x + \xo 15:13: \xt Exo 1:1-14; Acts 7:6.\x*
\v 14 \add But just as certain\add*, I'll¦6038 punish the¦6034 nation¦6034 that they serve¦6036 and¦6031 after¦6039 that they'll¦6036 come¦6042 out¦6042 with¦6043 many possessions¦6043.\x + \xo 15:14: \xt Exo 12:40-41; Acts 7:7.\x*
\v 15 And¦6046 \add as for\add* you, you'll go¦6047 to¦6048 your¦6050 ancestors¦6050 in¦6051 peace¦6051—you'll be¦6052 buried¦6052 at¦6051 a good¦6054 old¦6053 age¦6053.
\v 16 Then¦6056 in the fourth¦6057 generation¦6056 \add your descendants\add* will¦6058 come back here, because¦6060 the Amorites' sins won't¦6061 be complete¦6063 until¦6066 then¦6056.”
\p
\v 17 Then¦6070 the¦6071 sun¦6071 went¦6072 down and darkness¦6073 came, and wow, there was¦6074 a smoking fire¦6076 pot¦6076 and a flaming torch¦6078 that¦6080 passed¦6081 between¦6082 those¦6084 \add animal halves\add*.
\v 18 On that¦6100 day¦6086 Yahweh¦6089 made¦6088 an agreement¦6093 with¦6090 Abram¦6092, saying¦6094, “I've given¦6096 this¦6100 land¦6099 to your¦6095 descendants¦6095, from¦6101 Egypt's¦6102 river¦6101 to the¦6099 famous Euphrates¦6109 River.\x + \xo 15:18: \xt Acts 7:5.\x*
\v 19 \add That includes the land of\add* the Kenites¦6113, the Kenizzites¦6116, the Kadmonites¦6118,
\v 20 the Hittites¦6122, the Perizzites¦6125, the Refaim¦6128,
\v 21 the Amorites¦6132, the Canaanites¦6135, the Girgashites¦6138, and¦6130 the Yebusites¦6141.”
\c 16
\s1 Hagar and her son Yishma'el
\rem /s1 The Birth of Ishmael; Hagar and Ishmael
\p
\v 1 Now Abram's¦6146 wife¦6145 Sarai¦6144 hadn't been able to¦6149 give him¦6149 any children¦6148, but¦6144 she¦6148 had¦6148 an Egyptian¦6152 slave named Hagar¦6154,
\v 2 so Sarai said¦6156 to Abram, “Listen¦6177, Yahweh¦6165 has¦6164 prevented¦6164 me¦6164 from¦6166 having children¦6166 so please¦6163 sleep with my¦6172 slave¦6172. Perhaps¦6173 I¦6174 can have a family through her¦6175.” Abram agreed to what Sarai had suggested.
\v 3 So¦6182 Sarai¦6183, the wife of Abram, took¦6182 Hagar¦6189, her Egyptian¦6190 slave¦6191, after Abram had lived¦6195 ten¦6193 years¦6194 in¦6197 the land¦6197 of Canaan¦6198, and¦6182 gave¦6199 her to¦6201 Abram her husband¦6202 as a wife for¦6204 him¦6203.
\v 4 So¦6206 he¦6206 slept with¦6216 Hagar¦6209 and¦6206 she got pregnant¦6210, but¦6206 once she realised¦6211 that¦6212 she began to despise her¦6215 mistress¦6215.
\p
\v 5 So¦6218 Sarai¦6219 \add complained\add* to¦6220 Abram¦6222, “This is¦6224 all your¦6228 fault. I¦6225 let you sleep with¦6228 my¦6223 slave¦6227, but¦6218 now that¦6230 she's¦6231 pregnant she looks down on¦6228 me. May¦6234 Yahweh¦6235 judge¦6234 between¦6236 me and¦6218 you.”
\p
\v 6 “Listen,” Abram¦6241 replied¦6240, “She's¦6253 \em your¦6252\em* slave¦6246 to¦6242 do¦6248 what she's¦6255 told. Do¦6248 whatever you¦6252 think best.” So Sarai¦6244 started mistreating¦6253 Hagar, and¦6253 so she ran¦6255 away¦6255.
\p
\v 7 Then¦6258 Yahweh's¦6260 messenger¦6259 found¦6258 her¦6258 in¦6265 the wilderness¦6265 at¦6265 a spring—the spring beside the road to Shur¦6270,
\v 8 and \add asked\add* her, “Hagar¦6273, Sarai's¦6275 slave, where have¦6279 you come¦6279 from¦6283 and where are¦6281 you going¦6281?”
\p “I¦6286 am¦6287 running away from Sarai, my¦6285 mistress¦6285,” she¦6282 \add ≈replied¦6272\add*.
\p
\v 9 Then¦6289 Yahweh's¦6292 messenger¦6291 \add instructed\add* her¦6299, “Return¦6293 to¦6294 your¦6296 mistress¦6296 and¦6297 do whatever she tells you,”
\v 10 then¦6301 added, “I'll¦6306 give you so many descendants that they won't¦6310 even be able to¦6302 be counted¦6311 because there'll be so many.”
\v 11 Then¦6314 the¦6316 messenger¦6316 told her¦6315,
\q1 “Listen here¦6318: you're¦6318 pregnant¦6319 and¦6320 will¦6319 give birth to¦6329 a son¦6321,
\q1 and you'll¦6320 name¦6323 him ‘Yishma'el¦6324’ (\add which means ‘God hears’)\add*
\q2 because¦6325 Yahweh¦6317 has¦6327 heard your¦6331 cries of¦6331 misery.
\q1
\v 12 He'll be¦6334 a wild¦6335 donkey¦6335 of¦6335 a man¦6336
\q2 and¦6339 he'll¦6334 be hostile to everyone¦6338
\q2 and everyone will¦6348 be against him¦6341.
\q1 He'll \add live\add* right in¦6338 front¦6344 of his¦6347 brothers¦6347.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦6350 \add Hagar realised that it was Yahweh\add* who had¦6363 spoken¦6360 to¦6355 her¦6355 \add and said\add*, “You're ‘The¦6364 god who sees me’,” because¦6359 she¦6360 \add thought\add*, “Did I¦6363 really¦6361 just see the back¦6364 of¦6365 the \add god\add* who sees me?”
\v 14 So¦6367 that's why that well between¦6376 Kadesh¦6378 and¦6379 Bered¦6380 is¦6376 \add now\add* called¦6370 ‘The well of the living one who sees me’.
\p
\v 15 Then¦6382 Hagar¦6383 gave¦6382 birth¦6382 to¦6384 a son¦6385 for Abram, and¦6386 Abram named him Yishma'el¦6395.\x + \xo 16:15: \xt Gal 4:22.\x*
\v 16 Abram¦6410 was¦6398 eighty-six¦6400 years¦6403 old when¦6404 Hagar¦6406 bore¦6404 Yishma'el¦6409 for him.
\c 17
\s1 Circumcision as a confirmation of the agreement
\rem /s1 The Sign of the Covenant; Abram Is Named Abraham; Circumcision, the Sign of the Covenant; The Covenant of Circumcision
\p
\v 1 \add Many years later\add* when Abram¦6414 was¦6413 ninety-nine¦6417 years old, Yahweh¦6422 appeared¦6421 to¦6423 him¦6427 and said¦6426, “I'm¦6428 the all-powerful God¦6430. Obey me and don't disobey
\v 2 and I'll¦6442 establish my¦6438 agreement¦6438 with¦6443 you and will cause you to have very many descendants.”
\v 3 Then¦6446 Abram¦6447 \add knelt down with his face to the ground\add* and¦6451 God¦6453 told him¦6452,
\v 4 “Listen, my¦6458 agreement¦6458 with¦6459 you is¦6459 that you'll¦6460 become¦6460 the father¦6461 of¦6461 many nations¦6463,
\v 5 so you'll no longer be called¦6467 ‘Abram¦6472’, but¦6465 \add now\add* your¦6471 name¦6474 will¦6467 be ‘Abraham¦6475’ \add (which means ‘father of many nations’)\add* because¦6476 I'm¦6481 making¦6481 you the father of many nations.\x + \xo 17:5: \xt Rom 4:17.\x*
\v 6 I'll¦6484 make¦6483 you¦6484 \add and your descendants\add* very fruitful¦6483 so that they¦6491 form nations¦6488 and some of them will¦6491 become kings¦6489.
\p
\v 7 I'll establish¦6493 my¦6496 agreement with you¦6498 and your future descendants for¦6502 all the following generations¦6502. It will¦6493 be an agreement that never ends, that I'll be the your god¦6507 and God¦6507 of¦6508 your future descendants.\x + \xo 17:7: \xt Luk 1:55.\x*
\v 8 I'll give¦6511 this land¦6517 that you're staying in—the entire¦6520 region¦6517 of¦6517 Canaan¦6523—to you and your¦6518 descendants as a permanent¦6525 possession¦6524, and I'll be¦6526 their god¦6528.”\x + \xo 17:8: \xt Acts 7:5.\x*
\rem /s1 The Sign of Circumcision
\p
\v 9 Then¦6530 God¦6531 told Abraham¦6534, “\add For your part,\add*, you and¦6530 your descendants after¦6542 you throughout¦6543 \add all\add* their¦6543 generations¦6543 must¦6539 follow the requirements of¦6543 our agreement¦6538.
\v 10 This¦6545 is¦6546 the agreement¦6546 that¦6547 you and¦6550 all your future descendants are to¦6555 follow: every¦6556 male¦6558 among you must¦6548 be¦6554 circumcised¦6554.\x + \xo 17:10: \xt Acts 7:8; Rom 4:11.\x*
\v 11 This¦6561 removal of¦6562 the foreskin¦6563 will¦6560 be¦6560 a \add physical mark confirming\add* the agreement¦6566 between¦6567 me¦6567 and¦6564 you¦6568.
\v 12 All¦6585 male¦6578 babies must¦6574 be¦6574 circumcised¦6574 when they're eight¦6572 days¦6573 old. This includes all¦6585 those born¦6580 in your own house¦6581, as well as any that¦6589 have been bought¦6582 from¦6585 foreigners¦6588 even if they're not¦6590 your \add biological\add* descendants.
\v 13 \add Yes,\add* they definitely must¦6596 be circumcised¦6594 either way if they're born¦6597 in your house¦6598 or purchased¦6599 \add as slaves\add*. This way, my¦6602 agreement will¦6596 be manifested in your physical bodies as a never-ending agreement.
\v 14 Any males¦6609 who¦6610 isn't¦6611 circumcised¦6613 must¦6613 be¦6613 excluded from¦6621 his people¦6621 because he¦6625 will¦6613 have¦6625 broken¦6625 my¦6624 agreement¦6624.”
\rem /s1 Sarai Is Named Sarah
\p
\v 15 God¦6629 \add also\add* told Abraham¦6632, “As for¦6642 your¦6634 wife¦6634 Sarai, don't¦6635 call¦6637 her Sarai \add anymore\add*, because¦6642 from now on her name¦6644 will¦6637 be ‘Sarah¦6643’
\v 16 and I will bless her, and I'll also¦6648 give¦6649 you a son¦6652 from her. \add Yes,\add* I'll bless her and she'll¦6654 become¦6654 \add the mother of\add* nations¦6655—kings¦6656 of peoples¦6657 will come from her.”
\p
\v 17 Abraham¦6662 fell¦6661 to his¦6665 knees and he¦6666 laughed¦6666 and said¦6667 to himself, “How can a hundred¦6670 year¦6672 old man¦6670 father a child¦6681? And¦6674 what about¦6668 Sarah¦6676 who's ninety-nine¦6679 years¦6672 old having a baby!”
\v 18 Then¦6683 Abraham¦6684 said¦6683 to¦6685 God¦6687, “If¦6688 only \add you'd bless\add* Yishma'el¦6689 \add as my heir\add*.”
\p
