\p
\v 1 Then \add one day\add* Yahweh¦6846 appeared¦6844 \add again\add* to¦6845 Abraham at the oak trees¦6847 on¦6847 Mamre's¦6848 \add land\add*, while \add Abraham\add* was¦6850 sitting¦6850 at the entrance of his tent¦6853 during the hottest part of the day.
\v 2 \add Abraham\add* looked up¦6857 and \add was surprised\add* to see three¦6861 men¦6862 standing¦6863 \add a short distance away\add*. He¦6857 ran¦6866 from¦6868 the¦6868 tent¦6869 opening¦6868 to meet¦6867 them¦6867 and bowed¦6870 \add respectfully\add*,\x + \xo 18:2a: \xt Heb 13:2.\x*
\v 3 and¦6873 said¦6873, “My¦6874 masters¦6874, if¦6875 I've¦6878 found¦6878 favour¦6879 in¦6880 your eyes¦6880, please¦6877 don't¦6881 \add just carry on\add* past your slave¦6886.
\v 4 Let¦6888 me get some water¦6893 so that you can wash¦6894 your¦6895 feet¦6895 and¦6894 rest \add here\add* under¦6897 this tree¦6898.
\v 5 I'll go and¦6900 get some food¦6903 so¦6912 that you can refresh¦6904 yourselves¦6905 before you leave, since you've¦6921 come to your slave¦6916.”
\p “Alright, do¦6919 as¦6920 you¦6921 have¦6921 said¦6921,” they¦6917 \add ≈answered¦6917\add*.
\p
\v 6 So¦6923 Abraham¦6924 hurried¦6923 into the¦6925 tent¦6925 and told Sarah¦6928, “Quickly¦6930, \add grind\add* three¦6931 measures of fine¦6934 flour¦6934 and knead¦6935 it¦6929 and make¦6936 some bread¦6937.”
\v 7 He¦6956 ran¦6942 to the¦6941 herd¦6941 and selected a tender¦6948 and choice¦6949 calf and took¦6944 it to a slave¦6953 who hurried¦6954 to prepare it.
\v 8 Then¦6958 he took¦6958 yogurt and milk¦6960 and the calf that¦6964 had¦6965 been prepared¦6965, and he set \add the meal\add* down in front¦6967 of¦6961 the \add visitors\add*, standing¦6970 \add there\add* under¦6972 the tree¦6973 by them¦6967 while they¦6974 ate¦6974.
\p
\v 9 Then¦6976 they¦6976 \add asked\add* him¦6977, “Where's¦6979 your wife¦6981 Sarah¦6980?”
\p “See¦6983, over there¦6983 in¦6984 the tent¦6984,” he¦6982 \add ≈replied¦6976\add*.
