\v 10 “I'll¦6988 definitely return¦6987 to¦6989 you¦6989 here \add in the spring next year\add*,” the visitor continued¦6986. “You¦6989 see, your wife¦6996 Sarah¦6995 will¦6988 have a son¦6994 \add then\add*.”\x + \xo 18:10: \xt Rom 9:9.\x*
\p Now Sarah was at the opening¦6999 of¦6999 the tent¦7000 listening¦6998, but¦6986 the visitor was facing the other direction.
\v 11 Abraham and Sarah were¦7006 pretty old¦7006 \add at this stage\add* and Sarah had¦7009 passed the¦7008 age of being able to¦7010 have children,
\v 12 so \add when she heard that\add*, she laughed¦7015 to¦7018 herself and¦7025 said¦7018, “Now that \add my body's\add* worn¦7020 out¦7020, will I¦7020 have¦7021 the pleasure¦7024 \add of a child\add*? \add Even\add* my master's¦7025 \add too\add* old¦7026.”\x + \xo 18:12: \xt 1Pe 3:6.\x*
\p
\v 13 Then¦7028 Yahweh¦7029 spoke¦7028 to¦7030 Abraham¦7032, “Why is it¦7028 that¦7034 Sarah¦7036 laughed¦7035, saying¦7028, ‘Will¦7040 I really¦7039 have a child¦7040 when I'm¦7042 old¦7042?’
\v 14 Is anything¦7046 too¦7044 hard for¦7045 Yahweh¦7045? I'll¦7048 return¦7048 \add here\add* to¦7047 you¦7049 \add next year in the spring\add* and¦7052 Sarah¦7052 will¦7048 have a son¦7053.”\x + \xo 18:14: \xt Luk 1:37.\x*
