\p
\v 16 Then¦7070 the¦7072 \add three\add* men¦7072 got up \add to leave\add* and looked¦7073 down¦7073 toward Sodom¦7077, and Abraham¦7078 went with¦7080 them to \add see\add* them off¦7081.
\v 17 Then¦7083 Yahweh¦7083 said¦7084 \add to himself\add*, “Should I hide what I'm¦7089 about¦7090 to do¦7090 from¦7087 Abraham¦7087?
\v 18 \add His descendants\add* are certainly going to¦7095 become¦7093 a great¦7096 and mighty¦7097 nation¦7095, and all¦7100 the nations¦7101 of¦7101 the earth¦7102 will¦7098 be¦7098 blessed¦7098 through him¦7099 \add and them\add*,
\v 19 because¦7104 I'm aware that he'll command¦7108 his children¦7111 and his household¦7114 after¦7115 him, and they'll¦7116 follow Yahweh's¦7118 path¦7117 by their right¦7120 and just behaviour, so¦7122 that Yahweh will¦7123 bring¦7123 about¦7111 for¦7119 Abraham¦7127 what he's¦7131 said to him.”
\p
\v 20 Then¦7134 Yahweh¦7135 said¦7134, “Because¦7139 there's \add so many people\add* crying out about¦7136 Sodom¦7137 and Amorah¦7138 \add !(Gomorrah¦7138)\add*, and because¦7139 their¦7142 sin¦7142 is¦7144 very grievous,
\v 21 I'll go¦7147 down¦7147 \add there\add* now and see¦7150 if what I've heard about¦7151 them is true, and if not¦7159, I'll also¦7150 find that¦7152 out.”
\p
\v 22 Then¦7162 the¦7164 \add other two\add* men¦7164 left and started descending toward¦7166 Sodom¦7166, and Abraham¦7167 was¦7169 still¦7168 standing¦7169 there¦7163 in¦7170 front¦7170 of¦7170 Yahweh¦7171,
\v 23 so he¦7173 went¦7173 closer \add to Yahweh\add* and¦7175 asked, “Will¦7177 you¦7177 really destroy obedient people along with¦7179 those who are evil?
\v 24 What if there¦7184 were fifty people in¦7199 the city \add who've obeyed you\add*? Would you really¦7189 destroy the city and all its¦7199 people and not¦7191 save it for¦7195 the sake¦7195 of¦7195 those fifty?
\v 25 Surely you wouldn't do anything like that—killing the good people along with¦7209 the evil ones, so that they all¦7218 just¦7206 get treated the same? Certainly you wouldn't do that? Wouldn't the one who judges¦7217 the entire¦7218 world be¦7201 more fair?”
\p
\v 26 “If¦7227 I find¦7229 fifty¦7231 godly¦7232 people in¦7230 Sodom¦7230,” Yahweh¦7226 answered¦7225, “then¦7225 I'll¦7229 spare¦7235 the¦7233 whole city¦7234 for¦7239 their¦7239 sake.”
\p
\v 27 “Listen¦7244, I've¦7247 been bold enough to¦7248 \add question\add* my¦7251 master¦7251, even though I'm¦7252 \add just\add* dust¦7253 and¦7241 ashes¦7254,” Abraham¦7242 said¦7243 again.
\v 28 “Suppose they're five short of the fifty¦7258? Would you¦7261 destroy¦7261 the whole¦7265 city¦7267 because of five?”
\p “I won't¦7269 destroy it¦7268 if¦7271 I find¦7273 forty-five¦7275 there¦7274,” he¦7268 replied¦7268.
\p
\v 29 Abraham continued¦7282 to¦7280 make his request, “Suppose there's¦7285 forty¦7286 there?”
\p “I¦7289 won't¦7288 do¦7289 it¦7287 for the sake of¦7290 the forty,” he¦7278 agreed.
\p
\v 30 My master¦7298, don't¦7294 get angry but¦7293 let¦7297 me¦7299 speak¦7299,” Abraham said¦7293, “suppose thirty¦7303 are found¦7301 there¦7302?”
\p “I won't¦7294 do¦7306 it¦7304 if¦7307 I find¦7309 thirty there,” he¦7293 said.
\p
\v 31 “Listen, I've¦7317 taken it¦7313 on myself to speak¦7318 to my¦7321 master¦7321,” Abraham asked again, “suppose twenty¦7325 are found¦7323 there¦7324?”
\p “I won't¦7327 do it for the sake of¦7329 the twenty,” he¦7313 agreed.
\p
\v 32 “My master¦7337, don't¦7333 get angry and¦7332 let¦7336 me¦7338 speak¦7338 one last time¦7341,” Abraham added, “suppose ten¦7345 are found¦7343 there¦7344?”
\p “I¦7348 won't¦7333 do it¦7336 for the sake of¦7337 the ten,” Yahweh¦7337 conceded
\v 33 and then¦7352 he¦7352 left and Abraham¦7353 returned¦7361 home.
\c 19
\s1 Sexual depravity in Sodom
\rem /s1 Sodom and Gomorrah; The Depravity of Sodom; The Sinfulness of Sodom
\p
\v 1 So¦7364 the two¦7365 messengers¦7366 arrived at Sodom¦7373 in the evening¦7368, and Lot was¦7370 sitting¦7370 at the city gate¦7371. When¦7364 Lot saw¦7374 them, he¦7374 got up¦7377 to meet¦7378 them and knelt down¦7379 in front¦7380 of¦7365 them with¦7368 his face¦7380 to the ground¦7381.
\v 2 Then he¦7383 said¦7383, “Listen, my masters¦7387: Come with¦7404 me to¦7390 your slave's¦7393 home and wash¦7395 your feet¦7396 and stay¦7394 the¦7405 night¦7394. Then you can get up early¦7397 and continue on¦7404 your way¦7400.”
\p But¦7383 they¦7401 said, “No¦7402, rather we'll¦7405 \add just\add* spend¦7394 the night in¦7404 the street.”
\v 3 However, Lot insisted, so they followed him¦7412 \add off the main road\add* and went¦7413 into¦7414 his¦7416 house¦7416. Then¦7407 he¦7421 prepared a feast¦7419 for¦7418 them¦7418 and baked¦7421 unleavened¦7420 bread¦7420, and they ate¦7422.
\p
\v 4 \add However,\add* before¦7424 they¦7425 \add went to bed\add*, the men¦7426 of Sodom¦7429 surrounded¦7430 the house¦7433—there were young¦7434 and¦7435 old¦7437 from¦7434 all¦7438 parts of the city¦7427—
\v 5 and¦7443 they¦7443 called¦7443 out to Lot¦7446, “Where¦7449 are¦7450 the¦7450 men¦7450 who¦7451 came¦7453 to your place tonight? Bring¦7456 them out to us¦7457 so¦7458 that¦7458 we¦7458 can ‘use’ them.”\x + \xo 19:5-8: \xt Jdg 19:22-24.\x*
\p
\v 6 So¦7461 Lot¦7463 went¦7461 out¦7461 to¦7462 them¦7462 at the entrance¦7464 \add of the house\add* and¦7465 shut the door¦7465 behind¦7467 him¦7467
\v 7 and¦7469 said¦7469, “My¦7473 brothers¦7473, don't¦7470 do¦7470 this evil¦7474.
\v 8 Listen, I've got two¦7480 virgin daughters¦7481. Please¦7478 let¦7487 me¦7487 bring¦7487 them out¦7487 to you and you can treat them however you like. But¦7492 don't¦7483 do¦7499 anything¦7502 to these¦7498 men¦7497, because¦7503 they've¦7485 entered my house \add and so I'm responsible for them\add*.”
\p
\v 9 But¦7512 they insisted, “Stand back!” Then they said¦7517 \add to each other\add*, “This guy came to stay with¦7529 us, and now¦7524 he's¦7522 judging us. We'll treat you worse than them¦7527!” Then they started pushing hard against Lot¦7530 and came closer¦7532 to break¦7533 down¦7533 the¦7534 door¦7534.
\v 10 But¦7536 the \add two visitors\add* reached¦7536 out¦7536 their¦7540 hands¦7540 and pulled Lot¦7544 into the house¦7546 and shut the door¦7549 \add again\add*.
\v 11 Then¦7552 they struck¦7559 the men who¦7555 were¦7557 at¦7560 the entrance¦7557 of the house¦7558 with¦7560 blindness¦7560—\add all of them\add* from¦7561 the lowly to the prominent men—so that they gave up trying to find¦7566 the door¦7567.\x + \xo 19:11: \xt 2Ki 6:18.\x*
\s1 Lot and family leave Sodom
\rem /s1 Lot Leaves Sodom; Sodom and Gomorrah Destroyed
\p
\v 12 Then¦7569 the men¦7570 said¦7569 to Lot¦7573, “Who¦7575 else belongs to you here¦7578, a son-in-law¦7579 or your sons¦7580 or your daughters¦7581 or anyone else who¦7583 belongs to you in the city¦7586? Take them out¦7587 from¦7588 this place¦7590,
\v 13 because¦7600 we're \add about to\add* destroy it¦7602. \add The people have repeatedly cried out to\add* Yahweh¦7607, so he's¦7608 sent¦7608 us¦7608 to destroy the¦7598 city.”
\p
\v 14 Then¦7612 Lot¦7613 went¦7612 out and spoke¦7614 to his \add future\add* sons-in-law¦7618 who¦7620 were¦7620 \add engaged\add* to his daughters¦7621, and he told them, “\add Hurry\add*, get out of¦7618 this¦7628 place¦7627, because¦7629 Yahweh¦7632 is¦7631 going to destroy¦7631 the¦7635 city¦7635!” But¦7612 they thought he was¦7636 just¦7628 joking.
\p
\v 15 At dawn¦7642 the next day, the \add two\add* messengers¦7645 urged¦7644 Lot¦7646, saying¦7647, “Get up¦7643, take¦7649 your wife¦7652 and¦7641 your two daughters¦7656 who¦7657 are¦7657 here, so that all of you¦7660 won't be¦7660 swept¦7660 away¦7660 in¦7646 the punishment¦7661 of the city¦7662.”
\v 16 When¦7664 Lot hesitated¦7664, because of Yahweh's¦7676 mercy¦7675 for him¦7677, the men¦7667 grabbed his hand and his wife's¦7671 hand and the hands¦7672 of their daughters¦7674, and led them out¦7678 beyond the edge of the city¦7681.\x + \xo 19:16: \xt 2Pe 2:7.\x*
\v 17 At that point \add one of them\add* told Lot, “Flee for your¦7691 lives! Don't¦7692 \add turn around and\add* look¦7694 behind¦7695 you and don't stop¦7698 anywhere \add down\add* in¦7699 the plain¦7701. Escape¦7688 \add up to\add* the hills so you don't get swept¦7706 away¦7706!”
\p
\v 18 \add But\add* Lot¦7709 \add argued\add*, “Not right now, my¦7714 masters¦7714.
\v 19 Listen, you've¦7726 been kind to me and show us mercy by¦7728 saving¦7728 my¦7731 life¦7731, but¦7723 I won't¦7733 be able¦7734 to make¦7723 it¦7739 to the hills because the disaster¦7740 will¦7741 overtake¦7739 me and I'll¦7741 die¦7741.
\v 20 Listen, there's a small town¦7746 nearby that¦7747 I could¦7759 flee¦7749 to¦7749. Let¦7753 me¦7753 escape¦7753 there. It's¦7758 only small. Then my¦7760 life¦7760 would be saved¦7759.”
\p
\v 21 “Okay then¦7762,” the man replied¦7762, “I'll also¦7767 grant your¦7766 request about this¦7769 so I won't¦7770 overthrow¦7771 the town¦7774 that¦7775 you're talking about.
\v 22 Hurry¦7778 up, escape¦7779 there, because¦7781 I¦7783 am not¦7782 able¦7783 to do¦7784 a thing until¦7786 you¦7788 go¦7788 there.”
\p That's why they \add renamed\add* the¦7794 town¦7796 to ‘Zoar¦7797’ \add (which means ‘small’)\add*.
\s1 The destruction of Sodom and Amorah (Gomorrah)
\rem /s1 The Destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah
\p
\v 23 The¦7803 sun¦7799 had already risen by the¦7803 time Lot¦7804 \add and family\add* reached Zoar¦7806.
\v 24 Then¦7808 Yahweh¦7819 rained burning¦7817 sulfur¦7816 down onto Sodom¦7812 and¦7808 Amorah¦7815 \add !(Gomorrah¦7815)\add*,\x + \xo 19:24-25: \xt Mat 10:15; 11:23-24; Luk 10:12; 17:29; 2Pe 2:6; Yud 7.\x*
\v 25 and he¦7824 destroyed those¦7828 cities¦7827 and all their inhabitants¦7836 as well, as all of¦7830 the plain¦7832 including¦7829 all the vegetation.
\v 26 \add But\add* Lot's wife¦7842 who was following him¦7843 looked¦7841 back and¦7844 she¦7841 turned¦7844 into a pillar¦7845 of¦7845 salt.\x + \xo 19:26: \xt Luk 17:32.\x*
\p
\v 27 \add Meanwhile,\add* Abraham¦7849 got up early¦7848 in¦7850 the morning¦7850 and¦7848 went to¦7851 the place¦7853 where¦7854 he¦7856 had¦7856 stood¦7856 before Yahweh¦7861,
\v 28 and he looked¦7863 down¦7863 towards¦7869 Sodom¦7867 and Amorah¦7868 \add !(Gomorrah¦7868)\add* and the land of¦7874 the plain¦7875. From¦7877 there he saw¦7876, wow, that smoke¦7879 was rising from the land like¦7881 a furnace¦7882 \add chimney\add*.
\v 29 So¦7884 it¦7884 was¦7884 that when God¦7886 destroyed the cities of the plain¦7890, he remembered¦7891 Abraham¦7895 and¦7884 had Lot removed out¦7896 of the middle¦7900 of the destruction when he destroyed the cities that Lot had been living in¦7885.
\s1 The sad origin of Moabites and Ammonites
\rem /s1 The Shameful Origin of Moab and Ammon; The Origin of the Moabites and Ammonites; Lot and His Daughters
\p
\v 30 Then¦7912 Lot¦7913 and his two daughters left Zoar and settled up in the¦7917 hills, because¦7920 he was¦7921 afraid¦7921 to¦7922 stay in Zoar. So¦7912 he lived¦7924 in a cave¦7925 \add up there\add* with¦7916 his two daughters.
\v 31 Then¦7930 the older girl said¦7930 to the younger¦7934, “Dad's old¦7936 and¦7930 there¦7938 isn't¦7938 a \add single\add* man¦7937 \add up here\add* to \add marry\add* us¦7941 like happens to \add other women\add* in the world.
\v 32 So¦7953 let's¦7948 get Dad drunk¦7948 and¦7955 then we can lie¦7953 with¦7954 him¦7954, so¦7955 that¦7955 at least we can have some descendants through¦7956 our¦7956 father¦7951.”
\v 33 So¦7960 then¦7959, they¦7959 got their¦7962 father to drink¦7959 wine¦7963 that¦7965 evening, and the¦7967 oldest daughter went¦7966 and lay¦7968 with¦7964 her father, but¦7959 he¦7974 wasn't aware of¦7971 her coming¦7966 or going.
\p
\v 34 Then the next¦7980 day¦7980, the older girl said¦7981 to the younger¦7985, Listen, last¦7989 night¦7997 I¦7988 lay¦7988 with my¦7992 father. Let's¦7993 get him drunk¦7993 again tonight then you go¦7998 lie¦7999 with him so¦8001 that¦8001 we'll give life to descendants through¦8002 our¦8002 father.”
\v 35 So¦8009 that¦8008 next evening also¦8013, they¦8005 got their¦8011 father¦8011 to drink¦8005 wine¦8012 and the¦8014 younger¦8014 girl went and lay¦8015 with¦8007 him¦8016, but¦8005 \add again\add* he¦8019 wasn't aware of¦8011 her coming or going.
\v 36 In that way, both¦8024 of¦8025 Lot's¦8027 daughters¦8025 got themselves pregnant¦8023 through their¦8028 father¦8028.
\v 37 Then¦8030 the eldest daughter gave¦8030 birth¦8030 to a son¦8032 and¦8033 she¦8033 named¦8033 him Moab¦8035 \add (which means ‘from my father’)\add*. (He's¦8036 the ancestor¦8037 of¦8037 the Moabites¦8039 to this day¦8042.)
\v 38 The¦8044 younger¦8044 daughter also¦8045 gave birth to a son and¦8044 she¦8050 named¦8050 him Ben¦8052-Ammi¦8054 \add (which means ‘son of my people’)\add*. (He's¦8055 the¦8062 ancestor¦8056 of Ammonites¦8059 to this day¦8062.)
\c 20
\s1 Abraham and Abimelech and Sarah
\rem /s1 Abraham Deceives Abimelech; Abraham and Abimelech; Abraham and Sarah at Gerar
\p
\v 1 Then Abraham¦8067 travelled from¦8066 there¦8066 to the¦8069 Negev¦8069 region¦8068 and he¦8070 settled between¦8071 Kadesh¦8073 and Shur¦8075, staying in¦8077 Gerar¦8077 for a while.
\v 2 Abraham¦8080 had told \add people\add* his wife¦8084 Sarah was his sister¦8085, so Abimelech¦8088 the¦8089 king¦8089 of¦8089 Gerar¦8090 sent¦8087 for Sarah and¦8091 took¦8091 her.\x + \xo 20:2: \xt Gen 12:13; 26:7.\x*
\v 3 \add But\add* God¦8097 came¦8096 to Abimelech¦8100 in a dream¦8101 in the¦8101 night¦8102 and¦8096 told him¦8104, “Listen¦8105, you're¦8105 \add as good as\add* dead because of¦8114 that woman¦8109 you took¦8112 because she¦8113 is¦8114 married¦8114 to a husband¦8115.”
\p
\v 4 Now Abimelech¦8117 hadn't gone near¦8119 to¦8120 her¦8120, so he¦8119 said¦8121, “My¦8122 master¦8122, would you¦8127 destroy a nation¦8123 even though it's¦8120 innocent?
\v 5 Didn't Abraham himself tell me¦8133 that she was his sister¦8134? And¦8136 she herself also¦8138 said¦8141 that he¦8143 was her brother¦8142. I¦8149 did¦8131 this¦8150 with a \add clear conscience\add* and¦8136 with \add clean\add* hands¦8148.”
\p
\v 6 Then¦8152 God¦8154 said¦8152 to him¦8153 in¦8155 the¦8154 dream¦8155, “Yes¦8175, I know¦8158 that you did¦8163 this¦8164 with¦8155 a \add clear conscience\add* and¦8152 indeed I kept¦8165 you from¦8170 sinning¦8170 against me¦8172. I didn't¦8176 allow you to touch¦8179 her¦8180 for that reason.
\v 7 So¦8182 now¦8182, return that man's¦8186 wife¦8184 because¦8187 he's¦8190 a prophet¦8189, and he'll¦8191 pray¦8191 for¦8192 you and you'll¦8202 live¦8193. But¦8182 if¦8194 you don't¦8196 return her¦8197, be certain that you and all¦8204 your people will¦8197 surely¦8201 die¦8201.”
\p
\v 8 So¦8210 \add King\add* Abimelech¦8211 got up early¦8210 in¦8212 the morning¦8212 and called¦8213 for all¦8214 of¦8216 his¦8216 slaves¦8216 \add to come\add*, and he¦8217 explained the entire¦8220 situation to them and they¦8225 were¦8225 very scared.
\v 9 Then¦8229 he¦8229 sent for Abraham¦8231 and asked him¦8233, “What have you done¦8236 to us? What did I¦8240 do to you that¦8252 you would cause all this trouble for me and my¦8248 people? What you did to me should never have happened.”
\v 10 Then¦8259 he¦8259 asked again, “What¦8268 were you thinking when you did¦8265 that¦8271?”
\p
\v 11 “Because¦8275 I¦8276 thought that¦8283 there's¦8278 probably no one around here¦8278 who \add obeys\add* God¦8281,” replied¦8273 Abraham¦8274 “so they¦8284 might kill¦8284 me¦8284 because¦8275 of¦8280 my wife¦8288.
\v 12 \add Besides that,\add* Sarah actually \em is\em* my¦8293 \add half-\add*sister. We have the¦8294 same father¦8296, but¦8290 different mothers¦8302, and¦8303 then¦8290 it¦8303 was her that I took as a wife.
\v 13 \add Later\add* when God¦8312 got me to leave my¦8332 father's¦8314 home, I¦8315 said¦8315 to her¦8316, ‘You¦8320 could do this¦8317 one kindness¦8318 do for¦8316 me: Everywhere¦8323 we¦8327 go¦8327, just¦8317 tell them that¦8319 he's¦8333 your¦8318 brother¦8332.’ ”
\p
\v 14 Then¦8335 \add King\add* Abimelech¦8336 returned¦8343 Sarah¦8346 his¦8347 wife¦8347 to¦8342 him and also¦8338 gave¦8341 him flocks and herds, and male¦8339 and female¦8340 slaves,
