\p
\v 1 Abraham¦9775 was¦9776 now getting very old¦9776, and¦9779 Yahweh¦9779 had¦9780 blessed¦9780 him in¦9784 every¦9784 way.
\v 2 Then¦9786 Abraham¦9787 said¦9786 to his oldest slave¦9790 in his household¦9792 who¦9793 was¦9793 in charge¦9793 of¦9802 everything that¦9796 belonged to him¦9798, “Please¦9801 put¦9799 your¦9802 hand¦9802 under¦9803 my¦9804 thigh¦9804,
\v 3 and I want you to vow by¦9807 Yahweh¦9807, the god of the heavens¦9809 and the god of the earth¦9811, that¦9806 you won't¦9813 select a wife¦9816 for¦9817 my¦9817 son¦9817 \add Yitshak\add* from¦9818 any of the Canaanite¦9819 women¦9818 in¦9807 this area where we're living¦9822.
\v 4 Rather¦9836, you¦9832 should go¦9832 \add back\add* to my country¦9828 and to my relatives, and find a wife¦9834 for¦9835 \add him there\add*.”
\p
\v 5 “Suppose the woman¦9845 isn't¦9842 willing¦9844 to come \add back\add* with me¦9847 to this¦9851 place?” the slave¦9840 asked. “Should I¦9853 take¦9852 your¦9856 son¦9856 back to the country that¦9851 you¦9862 came¦9862 from¦9863?”
