\v 6 “Make sure that you¦9872 don't take¦9868 my¦9875 son¦9875 back¦9872 there¦9876,” Abraham¦9867 answered¦9865.
\v 7 “Yahweh¦9878, the god¦9880 of the heavens¦9881, who took¦9883 me from my father's¦9885 house¦9884 and from the land of my relatives, and who spoke¦9889 to me and who promised me, saying¦9896, ‘I'll¦9898 give¦9898 this¦9902 land to your¦9906 descendants,’ he'll¦9904 send¦9904 his¦9905 messenger¦9905 ahead of you, and you'll¦9907 \add be guaranteed to\add* bring back a wife¦9908 for¦9909 my son¦9909 from there¦9910.
\v 8 If¦9923 \add it turned out that\add* the¦9916 woman¦9916 isn't¦9914 willing¦9915 to come \add back\add* with you, then¦9912 you're released from¦9920 this¦9921 vow \add to me\add*. \add But still in that case,\add* don't¦9914 take¦9927 my¦9925 son¦9925 back there¦9928!”
\v 9 Then¦9930 the slave¦9931 put his hand¦9934 under¦9935 the thigh¦9936 of¦9936 his master¦9938 Abraham¦9932 and¦9930 promised his \add that he'd follow those instructions.\add*.
\p
\v 10 Then¦9946 the slave¦9947 took¦9946 ten¦9948 of his master's¦9951 camels¦9949 and \add loaded them with\add* all¦9953 kinds of good¦9955 things¦9955 from¦9950 his master, and \add with his own slaves,\add* he¦9958 travelled to¦9960 the city¦9966 of Nahor¦9967 in¦9957 the Aram¦9962-Naharaim¦9963 \add region\add*.
\v 11 Then¦9969 on that first evening¦9978, he¦9969 made¦9969 the camels¦9970 kneel¦9969 down outside¦9971 the city¦9972 by the well¦9975. It was the time¦9977 that women¦9981 come out¦9980 to¦9973 fetch water¦9976,
\v 12 and¦9983 he¦9983 prayed, “Yahweh¦9985, God¦9986 of my master Abraham, please¦9991 cause it to¦9992 happen¦9989 right in front¦9992 of me today that you show kindness toward my master Abraham.
\v 13 See, I'm¦10002 standing¦10003 by this \add well\add*, and¦10008 the young women¦10008 from the city¦10010 will¦10011 be coming¦10011 out¦10011 \add here\add* to¦10012 fetch water¦10013.
\v 14 Let it¦10015 be that if¦10037 I say¦10018 to¦10019 a young¦10016 woman¦10016, ‘Please¦10022 let me have a drink¦10024 from your water jar¦10023,’ and she¦10025 says, ‘Sure, and I'll also¦10027 get more for your camels¦10029,’ let her be the¦10016 one you have appointed¦10032 for your slave¦10033 Yitshak¦10034. And¦10035 by¦10035 \add finding\add* her, I'll know¦10036 that you've¦10032 shown kindness toward my¦10043 master¦10043.”
\p
