\p
\v 32 But¦12421 Yitshak¦12423 asked him¦12422, “Which son¦12430 \add are\add* you¦12427?”
\p “I'm your¦12430 oldest son Esaw¦12432.” he¦12421 \add ≈answered¦12421\add*.
\p
\v 33 Then Yitshak¦12435 \add started to\add* trembled¦12434 \add badly\add* and he said¦12441, “Then who¦12446 was it that hunted¦12446 game¦12448 and brought¦12449 it to me¦12450? I ate¦12451 it all¦12452 just before¦12453 you¦12454 came¦12454 \add in\add*, and I blessed \add that man\add* and indeed, he'll¦12459 be¦12459 blessed.”
\p
\v 34 When Esaw¦12462 heard¦12461 \add that\add*, then he¦12467 let out a very loud and exceedingly bitter¦12470 wail, and \add then begged\add* his¦12475 father, “Bless¦12476 me¦12476 too, my father.”
\p
\v 35 But¦12482 Yitshak replied¦12482, “Your¦12487 brother¦12484 came¦12483 \add in and deceived me\add* and he's¦12486 taken¦12486 your¦12487 blessing¦12487!”
\p
\v 36 “\add Yes,\add* his¦12492 name¦12492 Yacob¦12493 \add (meaning ‘deceiver’) suits him exactly!\add*”\x + \xo 27:36: \xt Gen 25:29-34.\x* said¦12489 Esaw. “\add First\add* he took¦12500 my inheritance and¦12489 man, now¦12502 he's¦12503 also¦12494 taken¦12503 my blessing!” Then¦12489 he \add asked\add*, “Haven't you¦12508 \add at least\add* saved a blessing for¦12509 me¦12509?”
\p
\v 37 But¦12512 Yitshak¦12513 replied¦12514, “Listen, I've made him master¦12517 over you, and I've given¦12525 all¦12522 his¦12524 brothers¦12524 to¦12526 him as slaves¦12527. And¦12528 I've sustained¦12530 him with grain¦12528 and wine¦12529. So¦12512 then¦12512, what¦12533 \add else\add* can I do¦12534 for¦12531 you, my son¦12535?”
\p
\v 38 “My father, Did you \add only\add* have \em one\em* blessing¦12542 that you \add could give\add*?” Esaw \add asked\add*. “Bless¦12548 me¦12548 too, my father!” Then¦12537 Esaw sobbed loudly.\x + \xo 27:38: \xt Heb 12:17.\x*
\p
\v 39 Then¦12558 his¦12560 father¦12560 Yitshak¦12559 responded¦12561 and¦12561 said¦12561 to¦12562 him,\x + \xo 27:39-40: \xt Heb 11:20.\x*
\q1 “Listen¦12563, you \add and your descendants\add* will¦12566 live
\q2 away¦12564 from¦12564 the \add most fertile land\add* on the earth¦12565\f + \fr 27:39 \ft The Hebrew text is ambiguous here. It could mean: (1) “away from the fatness of the earth and away from the dew of the heavens from above.” or “in a place/region where the earth/land/ground is not rich/fertile and where there is very little dew/rain.” or “in a place/region where the land/soil is not good for farming and where there is not much rain.” or (2) “of the fatness of the earth and of the dew of the heavens from above.” or “in a place where the land is good/fertile for farming and where there is plenty of dew/rain.”\f*
\q1 in a place that doesn't get dew¦12568 from¦12564 the¦12564 sky.
\q1
