\rem /s1 Jacob Flees to Paddan-Aram; Jacob Flees to Laban; Jacob Escapes Esau's Fury
\p
\v 41 \add From that time onwards,\add* Esaw hated Yacob because of¦12601 the¦12603 blessing¦12595 that \add their\add* father had¦12597 blessed¦12597 him¦12597 with¦12601, and¦12588 Esaw said¦12599 \add to himself\add*, “My¦12610 father's¦12605 \add funeral\add* can't be that far away—\add after that\add* I'll¦12606 kill¦12606 my¦12610 brother¦12610 Yacob.”
\p
\v 42 But¦12612 Rebekah¦12613 got to hear about¦12616 Esaw's¦12617 \add plans\add*, so she¦12620 sent¦12620 for¦12631 her¦12618 younger¦12624 son¦12618 Yacob¦12622 and¦12612 told¦12612 him¦12626, “Listen, your brother¦12629 Esaw is¦12630 \add coping with what happened by\add* planning to kill¦12632 you¦12632.
\v 43 So¦12634 my son¦12635, listen¦12636 to what I'm saying: for¦12641 your own sake, \add pack\add* up and¦12638 flee¦12639 to my brother¦12645 Lavan's¦12644 place in¦12637 Haran¦12646
\v 44 and¦12648 stay¦12648 with¦12649 him¦12649 for a \add while\add* until¦12652 your brother¦12657 \add cools down\add*.
\v 45 When \add he's\add* no longer angry with you and¦12666 forgets¦12666 what you did¦12670 to him¦12671, then I'll¦12672 send¦12672 for¦12671 you from¦12674 there¦12674 \add so you can return here\add*. I \add don't want to\add* lose both¦12679 of you on the¦12662 \add same\add* day¦12680.”
