\v 3 And¦12746 may¦12745 the powerful God¦12743 bless¦12745 you and make¦12747 you fruitful¦12747 and multiply¦12748 you so that you become¦12749 a community of¦12750 peoples¦12751.
\v 4 May¦12753 he¦12753 give¦12753 the \add same\add* blessing¦12758 of¦12758 Abraham to you—to you and to your¦12763 offspring¦12761 with¦12762 you—so that¦12768 you will own¦12763 the land¦12766 where you've been staying and which¦12768 God¦12771 gave¦12770 to Abraham.”\x + \xo 28:4: \xt Gen 17:4-8.\x*
\v 5 Then¦12774 Yitshak¦12775 sent¦12774 Yacob \add away\add*, and he¦12779 went¦12779 to Paddan¦12780-Aram¦12781—to Lavan¦12784, the son¦12785 of Bethuel¦12787 the Aramean¦12788 and the brother¦12789 of Yacob and Esaw's¦12793 mother¦12791 Rebekah¦12790.
