\v 14 she¦19162 \add yelled\add* for¦19166 the other male slaves and¦19162 told them¦19166, “Look, he¦19169 brought¦19169 a Hebrew¦19172 \add here\add* man¦19171 to \add mock\add* at¦19174 us¦19174. He¦19175 \add tried to get me onto the bed\add*, but¦19162 I¦19179 yelled out¦19179 loudly.
\v 15 When¦19183 he \add grasped\add* that¦19185 \add I was screaming for help\add*, he left¦19190 his¦19191 cloak here and¦19183 \add just took off\add* outside¦19195.”
\p
\v 16 \add Potifar's wife\add* kept the cloak beside¦19199 her until¦19200 \add her husband\add*, Yosef's master¦19203, got home¦19206,
\v 17 then¦19208 she¦19208 told him¦19209 \add the same story\add*, “\add That\add* Hebrew¦19217 slave¦19216 that you¦19220 brought¦19220 \add into our home\add* came¦19213 to me to \add mock\add* me,
