\p
\v 1 \add Sometime after that\add* the¦19344 Egyptian¦19354 king's¦19348 cupbearer and¦19351 baker¦19351 sinned¦19346 against their¦19352 master¦19352, \add also known as Far'oh\add*.
\v 2 Far'oh¦19357 was¦19356 angry¦19356 at those two¦19359 officials¦19360
\v 3 and¦19368 he¦19368 put them¦19369 in the custody¦19370 of the chief of the guards¦19373—in the prison¦19378 where¦19380 Yosef¦19381 was¦19382 \add also being held\add*.
\v 4 \add There\add* the chief of¦19386 the guards¦19387 assigned¦19385 Yosef¦19390 to serve¦19392 them¦19391.
\p After they'd been in¦19396 custody¦19396 for quite some time¦19395,
\v 5 the king's¦19411 \add cupbearer and baker\add* in¦19403 prison¦19416 each had \add separate\add* dreams¦19402 on¦19403 the same night¦19403, and each man's dream¦19399 had its own¦19402 interpretation¦19406.
\v 6 \add The next\add* morning¦19421, Yosef¦19420 came¦19418 to¦19419 them¦19419, and¦19418 wow¦19424, they¦19424 were¦19425 worried,
\v 7 \add so\add* he¦19427 asked¦19427 the¦19430 \add two former\add* officials¦19430 of¦19430 Far'oh¦19431, “Why¦19428 are you looking so upset today?”
\p
\v 8 “We¦19446 each had a dream¦19445 last night,” they¦19443 answered¦19443, “but¦19443 there's¦19448 no one¦19447 here who¦19447 can tell us what our dreams¦19445 mean.”
\p “God¦19454 is¦19448 the only one who gives someone the ability to¦19451 interpret¦19447 the meaning of dreams,” Yosef¦19452 replied¦19443. “Please¦19458 tell me¦19459 what you dreamed¦19446.”
\p
\v 9 Then¦19461 the chief¦19462 of the cupbearers¦19464 \add went first and\add* told his¦19467 dream to¦19468 Yosef¦19468, “Listen¦19465, in my¦19475 dream there was¦19475 a grapevine¦19474 in front¦19475 of me¦19475
\v 10 with¦19477 three¦19478 branches on it¦19482. Then¦19477 as soon as the buds appeared \add on the branches\add*, its blossoms¦19483 came¦19482 out \add straight away\add* and¦19477 its clusters¦19485 ripened¦19484 into grapes¦19486.
\v 11 Then¦19488 I was¦19490 holding Far'oh's¦19500 cup and I took¦19491 the grapes¦19494 and squeezed¦19495 them¦19496 into¦19497 it and I gave the cup to Far'oh¦19489.”
\p
\v 12 “This¦19513 is¦19514 the¦19515 interpretation¦19514,” Yosef¦19512 responded¦19510. “The¦19516 three branches¦19516 \add represent\add* three days¦19518.
\v 13 Within three¦19523 days¦19524, Far'oh will¦19525 \add display you publicly\add* and¦19530 then restore¦19530 you to your¦19533 position. Then you'll¦19534 place Far'oh's¦19526 cup¦19535 into his hand¦19538, \add just like you used to before\add* when¦19541 you were¦19542 his cupbearer¦19543.
\v 14 But¦19553 when it¦19551 \add all\add* goes¦19551 well¦19551 for¦19552 you, if¦19546 you remember¦19548 me then please¦19555 be kind and¦19558 mention¦19558 me to Far'oh¦19561 \add to\add* get me out¦19562 of this¦19566 \add prison\add*,
\v 15 because¦19568 indeed¦19570 I was¦19571 trafficked from¦19572 the land¦19572 of¦19572 the Hebrews¦19573. And¦19574 even here¦19576, I didn't¦19577 do¦19579 anything¦19580 \add to deserve being held in this\add* pit¦19585.”
\p
\v 16 \add Now when\add* the chief¦19588 of the bakers¦19590 saw¦19587 that¦19591 \add this first dream was\add* interpreted¦19593 \add so\add* favourably, he¦19593 told Yosef¦19597, “I¦19600 also¦19598 was in¦19601 my dream, and¦19587 listen, there were¦19606 three¦19603 baskets¦19604 of white¦19605 bread¦19605 on¦19601 my head¦19608.
\v 17 In¦19619 the top basket \add there\add* were \add various\add* kinds of food¦19613 for Far'oh¦19614—baker's¦19616 goods—but¦19610 the birds¦19617 were eating¦19618 them¦19619 out of the basket on¦19610 my¦19624 head¦19624.”
\v 18 “This¦19629 is¦19630 the¦19631 interpretation¦19630,” Yosef¦19627 responded¦19628. “The¦19632 three baskets¦19632 are¦19633 three days¦19634.
\v 19 Within three¦19639 days¦19640, Far'oh¦19642 will \add display you publicly\add* and then impale you on¦19649 a pole, and the¦19653 birds¦19653 will eat¦19652 your flesh¦19656 \add off your bones\add*.”
\p
\v 20 Then¦19659 \add three days later\add*, \add it was Far'oh's birthday\add* and he held a feast¦19670 for all¦19671 his¦19673 officials and he got the chief of the cupbearers¦19680 and the chief of the bakers¦19685 \add brought in to stand publicly\add* in the middle¦19686 of \add everyone\add*.
