\v 19 \add So\add* they¦21642 approached¦21642 the \add head servant\add* and¦21651 spoke¦21651 to¦21652 him¦21652 at the entrance¦21653 of¦21653 the house¦21654,
\v 20 \add explaining\add*, “Please, my¦21658 master¦21658, honestly, we¦21660 came¦21660 down¦21659 here the first¦21661 time¦21661 to¦21662 buy¦21662 food¦21664.
\v 21 \add But\add* when we \add got\add* to¦21670 \add our\add* lodging¦21672 place¦21672 \add that evening\add*, we opened¦21673 our sacks¦21676 and¦21666 \add got a shock because\add* each¦21680 man's¦21680 silver was in¦21681 the \add top\add* of his sack¦21676—the full amount of our silver was there. So¦21666 we've¦21685 brought¦21685 it¦21686 back¦21685 \add here on this trip\add*,
\v 22 plus we've¦21691 brought¦21691 more silver to¦21693 buy¦21693 food¦21695. We¦21697 don't¦21696 know¦21697 who¦21698 put¦21700 \add that\add* silver in¦21692 our¦21692 sacks¦21702.”
\v 23 \add But\add* he said¦21704, “Peace¦21705 to you—don't¦21707 be afraid. Your¦21712 god and¦21704 the¦21711 god of¦21711 your father¦21712 has given¦21713 you hidden¦21715 treasure¦21715 in¦21716 your sacks¦21716—\add I received your previous payment\add*.” Then¦21704 he brought¦21720 Simeon¦21724 out¦21720 to them¦21721.
\p
\v 24 Then¦21726 the \add servant\add* took the \add brothers\add* into Yosef's¦21732 house¦21731. He¦21726 \add had\add* water¦21735 \add given to them\add* and they¦21736 washed¦21736 their feet¦21737, and he¦21738 \add had\add* fodder¦21739 \add given\add* to their donkeys¦21740.
\v 25 Then¦21743 they \add got theirs gifts ready\add* for¦21751 when Yosef¦21749 would arrive at¦21750 midday, because¦21751 they'd heard¦21752 that¦21753 they would \add be given lunch\add* there¦21755.
\v 26 \add When\add* Yosef¦21760 \add arrived there\add*, they brought¦21762 \add their gifts\add* and¦21759 they bowed¦21771 to¦21763 the¦21766 ground¦21774 \add in front of him\add*.
\v 27 Then¦21776 he asked¦21776 them¦21777 about their \add living situation at home\add* and¦21776 \add questioned\add*, “Is everything ok for¦21777 your elderly father¦21781 that you \add ≈told me\add* about? Is he still¦21785 alive¦21786?”
\p
\v 28 “Things are well for your¦21790 servant¦21790 our¦21791 father¦21791. \add And yes,\add* he's¦21792 still¦21792 alive¦21793.” Then¦21788 they¦21788 bowed their heads¦21794 and¦21788 bowed \add to the ground again\add*.
\p
\v 29 Then \add Yosef looked around\add* and saw¦21802 his¦21801 full-brother Benyamin¦21805, and asked, “Is¦21811 this¦21811 your youngest brother that¦21811 you spoke¦21815 to me¦21816 about¦21801?” Then he¦21817 said¦21817, “May¦21819 God¦21818 be gracious¦21819 to you, my son¦21820.”
\v 30 \add At that point, Yosef had to\add* hurry out \add of the room\add*, because¦21824 \add he was so overcome with emotion for his younger\add* brother¦21830 that he needed to cry, \add so\add* he went¦21833 to \add his\add* inner¦21834 room and¦21822 cried there¦21836.
\v 31 Then¦21838 he¦21838 washed¦21838 his¦21839 face¦21839 and came¦21840 out¦21840, controlling¦21841 himself¦21841 and \add ordering\add*, “Serve the meal.”
\v 32 \add So the servants\add* served \add Yosef at his own table\add*, and served \add the brothers separately\add* and the Egyptians who were¦21857 eating¦21852 with him¦21853 \add separately again\add* (because Egyptians won't¦21856 eat¦21859 \add together\add* with Hebrews¦21862, because Egyptians \add would find that demeaning\add*).
\v 33 \add At their table, the brothers were astonished to discover\add* that they¦21870 had been seated in¦21876 order from the oldest to the youngest¦21874.
\v 34 Then¦21883 they were served¦21883 food \add Yosef's table\add*, but¦21883 Benyamin's¦21890 serving was¦21888 five¦21893 times larger than¦21891 any of¦21891 \add the others\add*, and they drank¦21895 and they and \add Yosef all\add* got a bit tiddly.
\c 44
\s1 Yosef frames Benyamin for theft
\rem /s1 The Missing Cup; Joseph's Silver Cup; Joseph Detains Benjamin; A Silver Cup in a Sack
\p
\v 1 Then¦21899 \add Yosef commanded his head servant\add*, “Fill¦21907 the men's¦21911 sacks¦21910 with¦21920 grain, as much as they¦21914 are¦21914 able¦21914 to¦21915 carry¦21915, and¦21916 put¦21916 each¦21919 man's¦21919 \add payment back into the top\add* of¦21917 his sack¦21921.
\v 2 And¦21937 put¦21928 my¦21925 \add own\add* silver¦21933 cup¦21925 in¦21929 the \add top\add* of¦21929 the youngest one's sack¦21930 \add along with his payment\add*.” So¦21923 he did \add what he was instructed\add*.
\v 3 The¦21943 \add next\add* morning¦21941 at daylight, the¦21943 \add brothers\add* and¦21946 their donkeys¦21946 were¦21944 sent¦21944 off¦21944 \add to start their trip home\add*.
\v 4 They¦21949 hadn't gone¦21954 very far¦21954 out¦21949 of¦21960 the¦21964 city¦21952 \add when\add* Yosef¦21955 \add ≈told his¦21960 head servant\add*, “Get up and¦21965, follow after¦21963 \add those\add* men¦21964. When you overtake¦21965 them, \add ask\add* them, ‘Why did you repay¦21969 good¦21972 with evil¦21970?
\v 5 Isn't this¦21975 \add the cup that\add* my¦21978 master¦21978 drinks¦21977 from and¦21980 indeed¦21981, what he¦21977 divines¦21981 with? You've done¦21984 evil¦21984 \add taking that\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 6 \add So the servant\add* overtook¦21988 them¦21988 and¦21989 \add did exactly what he'd been instructed to do\add*.
\v 7 But¦21996 they¦21996 \add asked\add* him¦21997, “Why does¦21999 my¦22000 master¦22000 \add say that\add*? Far¦22003 be¦22003 it¦22003 from¦22005 your¦22004 servants¦22004 to¦21997 do something like that.
\v 8 \add Listen\add*, we brought¦22015 the silver that¦22011 we found¦22012 in¦22013 the \add top\add* of our sacks¦22014 back¦22015 to¦22016 you¦22016 from the land¦22017 of Canaan¦22018. So \add why\add* would we \add then\add* steal¦22020 silver or¦22024 gold¦22025 from the house¦22021 of your¦22022 master¦22022?
\v 9 If you find¦22028 \add anything stolen with any of us\add*, \add that person can be executed\add*, and¦22031 \add the rest of us can also be taken as\add* slaves¦22037 for my¦22036 master¦22036.”
\p
\v 10 “Indeed,” the \add servant replied\add*, “according¦22043 to your words¦22043, \add that's how\add* it'll be: the one who is¦22048 found¦22048 with¦22049 \add the stolen cup\add* will become my slave¦22053, \add but\add* you others will be \add free to go\add*.”
\v 11 So¦22061 each \add of the brothers\add* quickly¦22058 lowered¦22059 his sack to¦22064 the ground¦22064, and¦22058 each one opened¦22065 his sack.
\v 12 Then¦22069 \add Yosef's servant\add* searched¦22069 beginning¦22071 with the oldest¦22070 and ending with the youngest¦22072, and the cup¦22075 was¦22074 found¦22074 in¦22070 Benyamin's¦22077 sack¦22076.
\v 13 \add Seeing this, the brothers\add* tore¦22079 their clothes¦22080 \add (as a sign of their distress)\add*, and each¦22082 one loaded¦22081 up his¦22085 donkey¦22085, and they¦22086 \add all\add* returned¦22086 to¦22087 the city¦22087.
\p
\v 14 \add When\add* Yehudah¦22090 and his¦22091 brothers¦22091 \add got\add* to Yosef's¦22093 house¦22092, he¦22089 was¦22096 still¦22095 there¦22096, and they¦22097 fell¦22097 \add to their knees and bowed\add* to the¦22092 ground¦22099 in front¦22098 of¦22091 him¦22098.
\v 15 “What's¦22104 this¦22107 that you've done¦22109?” Yosef¦22103 \add demanded\add*. “Didn't you know¦22111 that a man¦22116 like¦22118 me¦22118 can certainly divine¦22114 \add the truth\add*?”
\p
\v 16 “What can we say¦22124 to¦22125 my master?” Yehudah¦22121 \add ≈answered¦22120\add*. “What \add words\add* could we speak¦22128? How could we \add possibly\add* justify¦22131 ourselves¦22131? God¦22132 has¦22133 exposed the sin of¦22136 your¦22137 servants¦22137. \add So now\add*, we are¦22139 slaves¦22139 for my master—both we and¦22120 the one who¦22145 was¦22147 found¦22147 with the cup¦22148.”
\p
\v 17 “Far¦22152 be¦22152 it¦22152 from¦22154 me¦22164 to do¦22154 that¦22155.” Yosef \add corrected them\add*. “\add Only\add* the man¦22156 who had the cup¦22159 will¦22162 become my slave¦22165, and¦22151 \add the rest of\add* you can go¦22167 \add back\add* to your father¦22171 in¦22160 peace¦22168.”
\s1 Yehudah pleads to Yosef
\rem /s1 Judah Speaks for His Brothers; Judah Pleads for Benjamin's Release; Judah Pleads for Benjamin
\p
\v 18 Then Yehudah¦22176 went closer to¦22175 \add Yosef\add* and said¦22177 \add quietly\add*, “Please¦22182, my master, please¦22182 let¦22189 your¦22190 servant¦22191 speak¦22180 a word in¦22185 my master's¦22186 ears¦22185, and don't¦22187 \add get angry with me\add*, since you're \add as powerful as\add* Far'oh¦22194.
\v 19 My¦22198 master¦22196 \add previously\add* asked¦22197 his¦22200 servants¦22200 \add if we had\add* a father¦22205 or¦22206 another brother¦22208?
\v 20 And¦22210 we answered¦22210 to¦22211 my¦22213 master¦22213, ‘\add Yes,\add* we have an elderly father and \add also\add* the youngest¦22221 son of his old¦22218 age¦22220. But¦22210 \add that son's\add* brother¦22222 is dead, so he¦22223 \add alone is left of his mother's children\add*, and his father loves¦22229 him¦22229.’
\v 21 Then¦22231 you told your¦22234 servants¦22234, ‘Bring¦22235 \add the other son here so I can see\add* him¦22235 \add myself\add*.’
\v 22 And¦22241 we¦22241 said¦22241 to my¦22244 master¦22244, ‘The¦22248 young¦22248 man isn't¦22245 able¦22247 to leave¦22249 his¦22252 father¦22252, because if he¦22253 \add does\add*, then¦22241 \add the old man\add* will¦22253 die¦22257.’
\v 23 But¦22259 \add then\add* you said¦22259 to your servants¦22262, ‘If¦22263 your youngest brother¦22267 doesn't come¦22266 with¦22269 you, you won't¦22265 \add get access to me\add* again¦22271.’
\p
\v 24 “\add After all that,\add* when we went¦22277 \add back\add* to your servant¦22280 my father¦22281, we explained your words¦22286 to him¦22284, my master¦22287.
\v 25 \add Eventually,\add* our¦22290 father¦22290 \add ≈told us\add*, ‘Return \add there to\add* buy¦22292 \add some\add* food¦22297 for¦22294 us.’
\v 26 But¦22299 we \add ≈told him\add*, ‘We¦22301 can't¦22300 go¦22302 \add back unless\add* our youngest brother is¦22308 with us, because¦22310 we wouldn't be¦22313 able¦22313 to \add get access to that\add* man¦22316 if¦22303 our youngest brother wasn't with us.’
\v 27 Then¦22322 your¦22323 servant¦22323 my father¦22324 told us¦22325, ‘You know¦22327 that¦22328 my wife¦22333 gave birth to¦22332 two¦22329 sons¦22329 for¦22332 me¦22332.
\v 28 \add One of them\add* went¦22335 away from¦22337 me¦22337, and I've \add assumed that\add* he¦22341 was torn¦22341 to¦22341 pieces¦22341, and I've never seen¦22343 him¦22343 \add again\add*.
\v 29 So¦22348 if you also¦22349 take¦22348 this¦22353 \add son away\add* and¦22348 \add something happened to\add* him¦22356, then¦22348 you'd bring¦22358 my¦22355 grey¦22361 head down¦22358 to \add the grave\add* in¦22362 misery.’
\p
\v 30 “\add So\add* now¦22365, \add if I was to return home\add* to your¦22369 servant¦22369 my¦22370 father \add without that\add* young man, since his \add father's\add* soul is¦22375 bound¦22375 to his soul,
\v 31 then \add as soon as\add* he sees¦22379 that¦22380 the young¦22383 man¦22383 isn't¦22382 \add will us\add*, then he'll¦22384 \add have a heart attack\add* and¦22378 \add so\add* your servants¦22386 will bring¦22385 the grey¦22389 head of¦22389 your servant¦22390 our¦22391 father¦22391 down¦22385 to¦22393 \add the grave\add* in¦22392 misery.
\v 32 \add But\add* your¦22396 servant¦22396 guaranteed the¦22400 young¦22400 man¦22400 to my father, saying¦22403, ‘If¦22404 I don't¦22406 \add get\add* him¦22407 back to you¦22408, then I will¦22409 have sinned against my father all¦22411 \add my life\add*.’
\p
\v 33 “\add So\add* now¦22415, please¦22418 let your¦22419 servant¦22419 stay as a slave¦22422 for my¦22423 master¦22423 instead of¦22419 the young man, and¦22424 let the young man go¦22425 \add home\add* with¦22426 his¦22428 brothers¦22428.
\v 34 \add So now,\add* how¦22432 could I \add possibly\add* go¦22433 \add home\add* to my father if \add that\add* young man isn't¦22438 with me¦22439? I \add wouldn't be able to cope with\add* my father's¦22447 misery¦22442.”
\c 45
\s1 Yosef reveals himself to his brothers
\rem /s1 Joseph Tells His Brothers Who He Is; Joseph Reveals Himself to His Brothers; Joseph Makes Himself Known; Joseph Reveals His Identity
\p
\v 1 \add By now,\add* Yosef wasn't able¦22451 to control¦22453 himself \add in front of everyone who was standing around\add*, and¦22449 he called¦22457 out, “\add Send everyone else out!\add*” \add So Yosef was alone when he\add* revealed himself to his¦22472 brothers¦22472,\x + \xo 45:1: \xt Acts 7:13.\x*
\v 2 \add but\add* he¦22474 cried¦22478 so loudly that \add many\add* Egyptians¦22480 heard¦22479 \add it\add* and¦22474 Far'oh's¦22483 household¦22482 listened¦22481.
\v 3 “I'm¦22490 Yosef¦22486!” he¦22485 told his brothers. “Is¦22493 my¦22493 father¦22493 still¦22492 alive?” But¦22485 his brothers weren't able¦22497 to¦22499 answer¦22499 him because¦22501 they¦22502 were¦22502 terrified¦22502 \add there in front of him\add*.
\v 4 “Please¦22512 come close to me¦22513,” he said¦22515. \add So\add* they¦22514 came¦22514 close, and¦22505 he \add explained\add*, “I'm¦22516 your brother¦22518 Yosef¦22506 that you sold¦22521 \add to be taken to\add* Egypt¦22523.
\v 5 \add But\add* don't¦22527 be upset now¦22525 or troubled that you sold¦22536 me here, because¦22534 \add it was\add* God¦22542 \add who\add* sent¦22541 me ahead¦22543 of¦22540 you \add so that lives would be saved\add*.
\v 6 There's¦22556 \add already\add* been¦22550 two¦22548 years of¦22550 famine¦22549 in¦22550 this¦22547 region, \add but\add* there's¦22556 still¦22552 five¦22553 more years to come without any ploughing or harvesting¦22559.
\v 7 \add So\add* God¦22563 sent¦22562 me¦22562 ahead¦22564 of you all \add so that some of you would be kept alive by this miracle and your children would be\add* preserved¦22565.
\v 8 \add You see\add*, it wasn't you who sent¦22578 me here, but¦22574 God¦22582. And¦22583 he's¦22583 made me \add like a\add* father¦22584 to¦22584 Far'oh¦22585, and master¦22586 over all his¦22589 house¦22589 and the ruler¦22590 in¦22591 all the land¦22593 of¦22593 Egypt¦22594.
\p
\v 9 “\add So\add* hurry¦22596 \add back\add* to my¦22600 father¦22600 and¦22601 tell him¦22602, ‘This is what your¦22605 son¦22605 Yosef¦22606 says¦22604, “God¦22608 has¦22607 made me master¦22609 over all¦22610 Egypt¦22612. Come¦22613 down¦22613 to me—don't¦22615 delay¦22617.\x + \xo 45:9-11: \xt Acts 7:14.\x*
\v 10 You¦22619 can live in¦22620 the¦22620 Goshen¦22622 region¦22620 so that you'll¦22619 be¦22623 near¦22624 to me—you and your children and your children's¦22627 children and your flocks¦22630 and your herds¦22631 and everything that belongs to you.
\v 11 I'll¦22638 provide¦22638 for¦22638 you \add here\add* because¦22641 there's¦22640 still¦22643 five¦22644 years¦22645 of¦22651 famine¦22646 \add to come\add*. \add That way\add*, you won't \add end up poor\add*—you and your¦22651 household¦22651 and \add everyone with\add* you.” ’
\v 12 \add Look at me!\add* You \add yourselves\add* and¦22661 \add even\add* my¦22662 brother¦22662 Benyamin¦22663 \add can\add* see¦22660 that¦22667 it's \add really me who's\add* speaking¦22667 to¦22668 you¦22668.
\v 13 \add So go and\add* tell¦22670 my father about¦22671 all¦22674 my \add very high position\add* in¦22677 Egypt¦22677 and everything \add else\add* that¦22681 you've seen¦22682. Then¦22670 hurry¦22683 and bring¦22684 my father down¦22684 here.”
\p
\v 14 Then¦22690 he¦22690 \add hugged\add* his¦22696 brother¦22696 Benyamin and cried, and Benyamin cried \add too while they hugged\add*.
\v 15 Then¦22704 he¦22704 kissed¦22704 all¦22705 his brothers and cried over¦22709 them¦22709, and after¦22710 that his brothers talked with¦22714 him¦22714.
\rem /s1 Pharaoh Invites Jacob to Egypt
\p
\v 16 \add When\add* the report about¦22718 the arrival of¦22718 Yosef's¦22723 brothers¦22722 \add reached\add* Far'oh's¦22719 house¦22718, both¦22725 him and¦22716 his servants¦22728 \add were pleased\add*.
\v 17 Then¦22730 Far'oh¦22731 \add instructed\add* Yosef¦22734, “Tell your brothers¦22738, ‘Do¦22740 this¦22739: Load¦22741 your animals¦22744 and¦22730 leave. Go¦22745 to¦22732 Canaan¦22749
\v 18 and get your father¦22754 and your households¦22757, and come¦22758 \add back here\add* to me¦22759, and I'll¦22760 give¦22760 to you the best of the land¦22765 in Egypt¦22766, and you'll eat¦22767 the \add best\add* of the \add country\add*.’
\v 19 And¦22773 you're¦22774 commanded¦22774, ‘Do¦22776 this¦22775: Take¦22777 carts¦22782 with you from¦22780 \add here\add* for your little¦22783 ones and for your wives¦22784, and get your father¦22788 and come¦22789.
\v 20 Don't¦22792 \add be upset about anything you have to leave behind\add*, because¦22798 the best of¦22800 all¦22801 the land¦22803 in Egypt¦22804 \add will be yours\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 21 Then¦22808 Yisra'el's¦22812 sons¦22811 did¦22808 \add what they had been instructed\add* and¦22808 Yosef¦22815 gave¦22813 them¦22814 carts¦22816 as per Far'oh's¦22820 orders \add as well as\add* provisions¦22823 for¦22822 the¦22811 \add journey\add*.
\v 22 \add Then\add* he gave changes of clothes to each¦22826 of them¦22826, but¦22831 he gave three¦22833 hundred¦22834 pieces of silver¦22835 and¦22836 five¦22836 changes of clothes to Benyamin¦22831.
\v 23 To¦22840 his father he¦22841 sent¦22841 ten male donkeys loaded with the best of¦22840 Egypt¦22847, and ten female¦22849 donkeys loaded with grain¦22851 and bread¦22852 and provisions¦22853 for his father for the road.
\v 24 Then¦22857 he sent¦22857 off¦22857 his¦22860 brothers¦22860, and¦22857 as they¦22861 left, then¦22857 he told them¦22863, “Don't¦22858 quarrel on¦22867 the road.”
\p
\v 25 \add So\add* they¦22871 \add left\add* Egypt¦22870 and¦22869 \add went back home\add* to¦22874 their¦22877 father¦22877 Yacob¦22876 in Canaan¦22873
\v 26 and told¦22879 him¦22880, “Yosef¦22883 is¦22884 still¦22882 alive¦22884! \add In fact,\add* he's¦22887 the¦22891 ruler over all¦22889 of¦22891 Egypt¦22892.” But¦22879 \add Yacob was totally stunned and\add* he \add couldn't really\add* believe¦22898 them¦22899.
\p
\v 27 Then¦22901 they¦22901 told him \add everything\add* that Yosef had told them¦22910. \add When\add* he saw¦22911 the carts¦22914 that Yosef had sent¦22917 to carry¦22919 him, then¦22901 \add he started to recover from the shock\add*.
\v 28 Then¦22926 Yisra'el¦22927 \add exclaimed\add*, “Enough¦22928! \add I accept that\add* my¦22932 son¦22932 Yosef¦22931 is¦22933 still¦22929 alive¦22933. I'll¦22934 go¦22934 and¦22935 see¦22935 him¦22935 before¦22936 I die¦22937.”
\c 46
\s1 Yacob moves to Egypt
\rem /s1 Jacob Brings His Whole Family to Egypt; Jacob's Journey to Egypt; Jacob and His Family Go to Egypt; Jacob Goes to Egypt; The Israelites in Egypt
\p
\v 1 So¦22939 Yisra'el¦22940 started his trip, \add taking\add* everything he had. \add When they stopped in\add* Beer¦22947-Sheva¦22948, he offered sacrifices¦22949 to¦22947 the¦22951 god¦22951 of¦22951 his father¦22952 Yitshak¦22953.
\v 2 During the¦22959 night¦22960, God¦22956 spoke¦22955 to¦22958 Yisra'el¦22958 in¦22959 visions¦22959 sayings, “Yacob, Yacob.”
\p “I'm¦22966 \add listening\add*,” he¦22961 answered¦22955.
\v 3 Then¦22968 \add God\add* told \add him\add*, “I'm¦22969 God, the¦22971 god¦22971 of¦22971 your father¦22972. Don't¦22973 be¦22975 afraid¦22975 to go¦22976 down¦22976 to Egypt¦22977, because¦22978 I'll¦22972 make¦22982 you¦22982 into a great¦22981 nation¦22980 there¦22983.
\v 4 I myself will go¦22986 down¦22986 with you to¦22988 Egypt¦22988, and¦22989 I myself will also¦22989 surely bring¦22990 you \add back here\add*. And¦22994 Yosef¦22994 will \add be there with you when you die\add*.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦23001 Yacob¦23002 \add departed\add* from¦23003 Be'er¦23003-Sheva, and \add his\add* sons¦23006 carried¦23005 their father¦23012 and their little¦23015 ones and their wives¦23018 in¦23019 the¦23006 carts¦23019 that¦23020 Far'oh¦23023 had¦23022 sent¦23022 to¦23024 carry¦23024 him¦23025.
\v 6 They¦23027 \add had also brought along all\add* their livestock¦23030 and their possessions that¦23034 they had acquired in Canaan¦23037. Then¦23027 they \add arrived in\add* Egypt¦23039—Yacob¦23040 and all of¦23030 his¦23043 offspring with¦23044 him:\x + \xo 46:6: \xt Acts 7:15.\x*
\v 7 his sons and his sons' sons with him, and his daughters and his sons' daughters. So he¦23056 brought¦23056 all¦23053 his offspring with him to Egypt¦23058.
\p
\v 8 These¦23061 are¦23062 the¦23062 names¦23062 of¦23062 Yisrael's¦23065 sons who¦23066 went¦23066 to¦23067 Egypt¦23067, \add that is\add* Yacob and¦23069 his¦23069 sons: \bd Yacob\bd*'s firstborn¦23070 was Reuben¦23072,
\v 9 and \bd Reuben\bd*'s sons¦23074 were Hanoch¦23076 and Pallu¦23077 and Hezron¦23078 and Carmi¦23079.
\v 10 \bd Simeon\bd*'s sons¦23081 were Yemuel¦23083, Yamin¦23084, Ohad¦23085, Yakin¦23086, Zohar¦23087, and¦23081 Shaul¦23088, the¦23081 son¦23089 of¦23082 a Canaanite¦23091 woman.
\v 11 \bd Levi\bd*'s sons¦23093 were Gershon¦23095, Kohath¦23096, and¦23097 Merari¦23097.
\v 12 \bd Yehudah\bd*'s sons were Er, Onan, Shelah¦23103, Perez, and Zerah¦23105, but¦23099 Er and Onan had died¦23106 in¦23109 Canaan¦23110. Perez' sons were Hezron¦23115 and Hamul¦23116.
\v 13 \bd Yissakar\bd*'s sons¦23118 were Tola¦23120, Puvah¦23121, Yob¦23122, and¦23118 Shimron¦23123.
\v 14 \bd Zebulun\bd*'s sons¦23125 were Sered¦23127, Elon¦23128, and¦23125 Yahleel¦23129.
\v 15 Those were¦23133 \add all\add* Le'ah's¦23134 sons¦23133 that she¦23136 bore¦23136 for Yacob¦23137 in¦23138 Paddan¦23138-Aram, \add along with\add* his¦23142 daughter¦23142 Dinah¦23141. \add The total number of those descendants\add* was¦23148 thirty-three¦23148.
\p
\v 16 \bd Gad\bd*'s sons¦23151 were Zifion,Haggi, Shuni¦23155, Ezbon¦23156, Eri¦23157, Arodi¦23158, and¦23151 Areli¦23159.
\v 17 \bd Asher\bd*'s sons were Imnah¦23163, Ishvah¦23164, Ishvi¦23165, Beriah, and their¦23168 sister¦23168 Serah¦23167. And¦23165 Beriah's¦23166 sons were Heber¦23171 and Malkiel¦23172.
\v 18 Those were¦23175 \add all\add* Zilpah's¦23176 sons¦23175, \add the slave woman\add* that Lavan¦23180 had¦23179 given¦23179 to his¦23182 daughter¦23182 Le'ah¦23181, and¦23183 she¦23183 gave¦23183 birth¦23183 to those¦23186 sixteen \add descendants\add* for Yacob¦23187.
\p
\v 19 Yacob's¦23195 wife¦23194 Rahel's¦23193 sons¦23192 were Yosef¦23196 and¦23197 Benyamin¦23197.
\v 20 \bd Yosef\bd*'s sons Manasseh¦23216 and¦23199 Efrayim¦23219 were born¦23199 in¦23201 Egypt¦23202. Asenath¦23207, the daughter¦23208 of Potifera the priest¦23212 of On¦23213, gave birth to¦23200 them for¦23206 \add Yosef\add*.\x + \xo 46:20: \xt Gen 41:50-52.\x*
\v 21 \bd Benyamin\bd*'s sons¦23221 were Bela¦23223, Beker¦23224, Ashbel¦23225, Gera¦23226, Naaman¦23227, Ehi¦23228, Rosh¦23229, Muppim¦23230, Huppim¦23231, and¦23221 Ard¦23232.
\v 22 Those¦23239 were¦23235 \add all\add* Rahel's¦23236 descendants—a total of¦23235 fourteen.
\p
\v 23 \bd Dan\bd*'s son¦23246 was Hushim¦23249.
\v 24 \bd Naftali\bd*'s sons¦23251 were Yahzeel¦23253, Guni¦23254, Yezer¦23255, and¦23251 Shillem¦23256.
\v 25 Those \add two\add* were¦23259 \add both\add* Bilhah's¦23260 sons¦23259, \add the slave woman\add* that Lavan¦23264 had¦23263 given¦23263 to his¦23266 daughter¦23266 Rahel¦23265, and¦23267 she¦23267 gave¦23267 birth¦23267 to those¦23270 seven¦23275 \add descendants\add* for Yacob¦23271.
\p
\v 26 \add The total count of those\add* who went¦23280 to¦23281 Egypt¦23282 with Yacob¦23281 who \add were his descendants\add* (not counting \add his daughters-in-law\add*) was¦23293 sixty-six¦23293.
\v 27 \add As well as that\add*, Yosef's¦23297 two¦23305 sons¦23296 were¦23304 born¦23300 in¦23303 Egypt¦23303 so that \add added up to a grand total of\add* seventy¦23314.\x + \xo 46:27: \xt Acts 7:14.\x*
\s1 Yacob's arrival in Egypt
\rem /s1 Jacob and His Family in Egypt; Jacob Settles in Goshen; Jacob's Family Arrives in Goshen
\p
\v 28 \add As they all approached Egypt, Yacob\add* sent¦23320 Yehudah¦23319 ahead¦23321 \add of the others\add* to find out from Yosef¦23324 how to get to Goshen. \add As they all\add* arrived in the Goshen area,
\v 29 Yosef¦23333 \add hooked up\add* his chariot¦23334 and went to meet¦23336 his father Yisra'el¦23338 \add there\add*. He¦23340 \add went up to his father, and hugged him for a long time as he cried\add*.
\v 30 “Now I can die¦23358,” Yisra'el¦23354 said¦23353 to¦23355 Yosef¦23357, “since I've¦23361 seen your¦23364 face¦23364—\add seen\add* that¦23359 you're¦23366 still¦23366 alive¦23367.”
\p
\v 31 Then¦23369 Yosef¦23370 spoke¦23369 to his brothers and to his father's household, “I'll¦23378 go¦23378 and report to Far'oh¦23380 and \add explain\add* to him¦23382 that my brothers and my father's household who¦23387 were living in¦23388 Canaan¦23390 have¦23391 come¦23391 to \add join\add* me¦23392.
\v 32 \add I'll tell him that you're\add* herders of¦23395 sheep¦23396—livestock¦23400 \add farmers\add*—and \add that you've\add* brought¦23408 your flocks¦23402 and herds¦23403 and everything that \add you own\add*.
\v 33 So¦23411 when Far'oh¦23415 calls for¦23414 you¦23414 and¦23416 \add asks what your work is\add*,
\v 34 then¦23421 you should \add answer\add*, ‘Your¦23436 servants¦23425 have¦23424 been¦23424 livestock¦23423 men¦23422 from our youth¦23426 and until now¦23429, both¦23430 we¦23432 and also¦23427 our fathers¦23435,’ so that you can settle \add here\add* in¦23436 Goshen¦23439, because¦23440 Egyptians¦23443 \add despise sheep herders\add*.”
\c 47
\rem /s1 Jacob Blesses Pharaoh
\p
\v 1 Then¦23449 went¦23449 Yosef¦23450 to Far'oh¦23452 and told¦23451 \add him\add*, “My¦23454 father¦23454 and brothers¦23455 and their¦23456 flocks¦23456 and herds¦23457 and everything that¦23460 \add belongs\add* to them¦23461, have¦23462 come¦23462 from¦23463 Canaan¦23464 and they're \add here now\add* Goshen¦23467 \add area\add*.”
\v 2 Then¦23469 he¦23471 took¦23471 five¦23472 of¦23475 his brothers¦23470 and¦23469 presented¦23474 them¦23474 to¦23475 Far'oh¦23476,
\v 3 and¦23486 Far'oh¦23479 \add asked them\add*, “What's¦23483 your¦23492 occupation¦23485?”
\p “Your¦23492 servants¦23492 have been shepherds \add for several generations\add*,” they¦23486 \add ≈replied¦23478\add*.
\v 4 Then¦23500 they¦23500 \add explained\add*, “We've¦23503 come¦23506 to¦23501 \add stay here for a while\add* because in Canaan¦23519, there's¦23509 no pasture¦23510 for our flocks¦23511 because \add the drought is very severe\add*. So¦23500 now¦23520, please¦23523 let¦23521 your¦23524 servants¦23524 settle in the Goshen¦23526 \add area\add*.”
\v 5 Then¦23528 Far'oh¦23529 turned to Yosef¦23532, “Your¦23534 father¦23534 and¦23535 your¦23535 brothers¦23535 have¦23536 come¦23536 to you¦23537.
\v 6 The¦23543 \add entire country\add* of Egypt¦23540 is in front¦23541 of you. Settle your father¦23548 and¦23549 your brothers¦23551 in the best¦23543 land¦23553, \add so\add* let¦23552 them settle in the Goshen¦23554 \add area\add*. And¦23555 if¦23555 you're \add aware\add* that¦23569 \add some of them have special talents\add*, then appoint¦23564 them as overseers¦23565 of \add my own\add* livestock¦23566 \add as well\add*.”
\p
\v 7 Then¦23573 Yosef¦23574 brought¦23573 his¦23578 father¦23578 Yacob and presented¦23579 him¦23579 to¦23580 Far'oh, and Yacob blessed¦23582 Far'oh.
\v 8 “How¦23592 \add old are you\add*?” Far'oh¦23589 asked him.
\p
\v 9 “\add I've been moving from place to place for\add* 130 years¦23608,” Yacob¦23599 \add ≈replied¦23598\add*. “\add My life has been short and with many difficulties, so I\add* haven't reached¦23616 the¦23619 longer \add ages of my ancestors in their moving around\add*.”
\v 10 Then¦23626 \add he\add* blessed¦23626 Far'oh¦23630 \add again\add* and¦23631 departed from¦23632 \add his\add* presence¦23632.
\v 11 So¦23635 Yosef¦23636 gave¦23643 his father¦23639 and his brothers¦23642 \add some of the best land\add* in Egypt¦23647 and \add helped\add* them¦23644 settle¦23635 there—in the Rameses¦23651 \add district just\add* as¦23652 Far'oh¦23654 had¦23653 commanded¦23653.
\v 12 \add He also\add* provided¦23656 his father and his brothers¦23663 and all¦23665 his father's¦23668 household¦23667 with bread—each¦23665 family according¦23670 to¦23670 the¦23670 \add number of children\add*.
\s1 Yosef's leadership through extreme famine
\rem /s1 Joseph's Leadership in the Famine; Joseph and the Famine; The Famine; The Famine in Egypt
\p
\v 13 \add Then the time came when\add* there¦23674 was no bread in¦23675 \add that entire part of\add* the world, because¦23678 the \add drought\add* was now extremely severe, and \add both\add* Egypt¦23685 and Canaan¦23687 were \add suffering from food shortages\add*.
\v 14 \add People all over came\add* to buy¦23708 grain¦23704, and \add over time\add* Yosef¦23692 had received \add in payment\add* all the¦23697 silver that¦23705 could be found¦23698 in Egypt¦23701 and Canaan¦23703, and \add he in turn\add* took it¦23709 to Far'oh's¦23715 house¦23714.
\v 15 So¦23717 \add once there was no more silver left\add* in Egypt¦23720 and¦23717 in Canaan¦23722, all¦23724 \add the Egyptians\add* demanded from¦23719 Yosef¦23729, “Give us food¦23734. Why should we¦23736 die¦23736 \add right here in front of\add* you¦23737? \add All our money\add* is gone!”
\p
\v 16 “Bring your¦23748 livestock¦23745,” Yosef¦23743 \add ≈answered¦23742\add*, “and¦23742 I'll give¦23746 grain to¦23747 you in¦23748 exchange for¦23747 \add them\add*, since the silver is gone.”
\v 17 So \add the people\add* brought¦23754 their livestock to¦23758 \add him\add*, and \add he\add* gave¦23761 them grain \add in exchange for their\add* horses¦23765 and sheep¦23767 and cattle¦23769 and donkeys¦23770. So he provided¦23771 them with¦23765 food¦23772 that¦23777 year¦23776 \add in exchange\add* for all¦23773 their livestock.
\p
\v 18 \add The next\add* year¦23780 they¦23782 came¦23782 to \add Yosef\add* and \add begged\add*, “We¦23790 can't¦23788 hide¦23790 it¦23795 from¦23791 our master¦23791 that¦23792 since \add there's no silver left\add* and \add since all\add* the¦23797 livestock¦23797 \add now\add* belongs to our lord, there's nothing left \add to offer other than\add* our bodies¦23809 and our lands¦23810.
\v 19 Why should we die \add right in front of you\add*—both we and our land? Buy¦23820 us and our land in exchange for¦23826 food¦23826, and we and our land will¦23827 be slaves¦23830 to¦23812 Far'oh¦23831. And¦23829 give¦23832 us seed¦23834 so that we'll¦23827 live¦23835 and not¦23836 die, and so that the¦23838 land won't¦23836 be barren.”
\p
\v 20 So¦23842 Yosef¦23843 bought¦23842 all the farmland of¦23848 Egypt¦23849 for¦23850 Far'oh, because every¦23855 Egyptian¦23854 sold¦23853 his¦23856 field¦23856. \add In that way, all\add* the land¦23863 became¦23862 Far'oh's¦23850 because the famine¦23861 was¦23859 \add so extreme\add*.
\v 21 \add As for\add* the people¦23868, he¦23869 moved them to the cities¦23871\f + \fr 47:21 \ft TC: There's a variation here in different early copies and translations. Rather than moving the people into the cities (which might have been done to make food distribution more efficient), some translations choose the alternative ‘made the people slaves’.\f* from¦23872 one end¦23872 of¦23872 Egypt¦23875 to the other¦23878.
\v 22 The¦23881 only¦23880 land he¦23884 didn't buy¦23884 was that¦23894 of¦23881 the¦23882 priests¦23882, because¦23885 they \add were given a regular allowance\add* by Far'oh¦23889. Because¦23897 they \add could live on what they were supplied with\add*, they didn't \add need to\add* sell¦23902 their¦23905 land.
\v 23 Then¦23907 Yosef¦23908 told the people¦23911, “Listen, now that I've¦23913 bought¦23913 you and¦23907 your land¦23918 for Far'oh¦23919, here¦23920 is¦23923 seed¦23923 for you so that you can \add work\add* the ground.
\v 24 \add Every time\add* you harvest¦23930 \add a crop\add*, you must¦23931 give¦23931 a fifth¦23932 \add of it\add* to Far'oh¦23933. The¦23935 \add other\add* four¦23934 parts¦23935 will¦23936 be for you \add to use\add* as seed¦23938 and as food¦23940 for yourselves¦23940 and your households¦23942 and your young children.”
\p
\v 25 “You've kept us alive¦23947,” they¦23946 \add agreed\add*. “Master¦23952, \add continue to show us your favour\add*, and¦23953 we'll¦23953 be¦23953 slaves¦23954 for Far'oh¦23955.”
\v 26 So¦23957 Yosef¦23959 established it¦23957 as a law to this¦23964 day¦23963 concerning the Egyptian¦23968 farmland: that¦23964 the fifth¦23970 belongs¦23976 to Far'oh. (Only¦23971 the priests' land¦23972 didn't¦23975 become Far'oh's¦23969.)
\s1 Yacob's burial request
\rem /s1 Jacob's Last Request; The Last Days of Jacob
\p
\v 27 So¦23979 Yisra'el¦23980 \add !(Yacob) and his descendants\add* settled in the Goshen¦23984 region¦23981 of¦23982 Egypt¦23982 and \add prospered\add*. The \add had many children\add* and \add quickly increased in number\add*.
\v 28 Yacob¦23992 resided \add there\add* for seventeen¦23995 years, and¦23991 \add by then\add* he¦23991 was¦23998 147 years old
